hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3001","3000 - So Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us: Abu Zayd Said ibn al-Rabi informed us: Shuba informed us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Masud."
"3002","3001 - And Salama ibn Shabib informed us of it: al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad informed us: Shuba informed us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Masud."
"3003","3002 - Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us: al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr informed us: Shuba informed us, from al-Rabi ibn al-Rukayn, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Masud."
"3004","3003 - And Salama ibn Shabib informed us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Masud. Abu Bakr said: And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn Yusuf; and al-Masudi narrated it from Qays, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Masud."
"3005","3004 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai informed us of it: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami informed us, from al-Masudi. So all of these agreed, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abd Allah ibn Masud. While Muhammad ibn Jabir said: from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abu Musa - so he erred in it, and he was poor in memory; and we mentioned these hadiths only to clarify the defect of this hadith."
"3006","3005 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Muawiya informed us: al-Amash informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3007","3006 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us: Yahya ibn Said informed us: Sufyan informed us: Sulayman informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""There is no one more patient over harm he hears than Allah, blessed and exalted: they ascribe to Him a son, while He grants them health and provides for them."" Abu Bakr said: And we do not know Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated from Abu Musa except this hadith."
"3008","3007 - And Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim informed us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Dawud informed us: al-Amash informed us, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And Abu Musa is Abd Allah ibn Qays; so he said: from Abd Allah, without attributing him."
"3009","3008 - Abda ibn Abd Allah informed us: Yahya ibn Adam informed us: Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid. 3009 - Abu Ahmad informed us: Israil informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, who said: Abu Musa said: Ali ibn Abi Talib reminded us of a prayer we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - either we forgot it or we abandoned it. He said: ""So he would say takbir when he bowed and when he raised his head from bowing."" Thus Israil narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad; while Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam."
"3010","3010 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali informed us, saying: Abu Muawiya informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who fights out of bravery, a man who fights out of zeal, and a man who fights to show off; so which of that is in the path of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is the highest, he is in the path of Allah."""
"3011","3011 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us: Shuba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3012","3012 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights to gain booty, and a man fights so his place is seen; so which of this is in the path of Allah? He said: ""Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is the highest, he is in the path of Allah."""
"3013","3013 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Muawiya informed us: al-Amash informed us, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa."
"3014","3014 - And Yusuf ibn Musa informed us: Jarir informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who loves a people but has not yet joined them? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man is with whom he loves."" And this hadith was narrated by Shuba from al-Amash, from Abu Wail, from Abd Allah."
"3015","3015 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Waki informed us: al-Amash informed us, from Shaqiq, who said: I was sitting with Abd Allah and Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with them both), and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Before the Hour there are days in which ignorance descends and in which harj increases."" We said: And what is harj? He said: ""Killing, killing."""
"3016","3016 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Khallad ibn Yazid informed us: Abd al-Malik ibn Humayd ibn Abi Ghaniyya informed us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he was asked: Which Islam is best? He said: ""One from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."" It was said: Then which jihad is best? He said: ""One whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed."" It was said: Then which prayer is best? He said: ""Long standing (qunut)."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abu Musa, except Abd al-Malik ibn Humayd ibn Abi Ghaniyya; while others besides Ibn Abi Ghaniyya only narrate it from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3017","3017 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Feed the hungry, visit the sick, and free the captive."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Wail, from Abu Musa, except Mansur; and more than one narrated it from Mansur."
"3018","3018 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us with four (statements) and said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, does not sleep, nor is it fitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the scale"" - Abu Bakr said: I think he said: ""and raises it. The deeds of the night are raised to Him by day, and the deeds of the day by night. His veil is light; were He to uncover it, the splendors of His face would burn everything His sight reaches."""
"3019","3019 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us: Abu Muawiya informed us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it - except that he said: ""He lowers the scale and raises it,"" and he said: ""Everything His sight reaches."""
"3020","3020 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra: I heard Abu Ubayda narrating from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3021","3021 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us: Abu Muawiya informed us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, extends His hand by night so that the evildoer of the day may repent, until the sun rises from its setting place."""
"3022","3022 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us: Jarir informed us, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he named for us names of himself; of them what we memorized. So he said: ""I am Muhammad and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, al-Muqaffi, and the Prophet of repentance and the Prophet of battle."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abu Musa, except Jarir; and al-Masudi narrated it from Amr ibn Murra."
"3023","3023 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us of it: Abu Dawud informed us: al-Masudi informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, from Abu Ubayda, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named for us names of himself; of them what we memorized. So he said: ""I am Muhammad and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, al-Muqaffi, and the Prophet of battle."""
"3024","3024 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Asim informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us: Ata informed me: Ubayd ibn Umayr informed me that Abu Musa sought permission from Umar three times but was not permitted, while he was busy. When he finished he said: Did I not hear Abd Allah ibn Qays? Permit him. It was said: He returned. He said: Call him. So he said: We were commanded with that. He said: We shall surely bring proof for that. He said: So he went to a gathering of the gatherings of the Ansar, and they said: None shall testify for you except the youngest of us, Abu Said al-Khudri. So he testified for him. So Umar said: Was this of the affair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hidden from me? The dealing in the markets distracted me; but ask me whatever you wish, and do not seek permission. And we do not know Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated from Abu Musa except this hadith."
"3025","3025 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray informed us: Awf informed us: Qasama - meaning Ibn Zuhayr - informed us: al-Ashari informed us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3026","3026 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it: Yahya ibn Said informed us: Awf informed us, from Qasama, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Allah, blessed and exalted, created Adam from a handful He grasped from all the earth; so his children came according to that: of them the white and the red and the black, and the easy and the hard, and the wicked and the good, and between that."" And these words, we do not know anyone who narrated them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Musa; and we do not know for them a path from Abu Musa except this path."
"3027","3027 - Khallad ibn Aslam al-Marwazi narrated to us: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us: Awf informed us, from Qasama ibn Zuhayr, from Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The example of the righteous companion is like the perfume seller: either he gives you of his perfume, or some of its scent reaches you. And the example of the evil companion is like the blacksmith: either he burns your garment, or he makes you stink, or his smell harms you."" And this hadith was narrated with this chain from Abu Musa, stopped (mawquf); and we do not know anyone who raised it except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl, from Awf."
"3028","3028 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi informed us: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman informed us: Awf informed us, from Qasama ibn Zuhayr, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The example of the believer who recites the Quran is like the citron: sweet its taste, sweet its scent. And the example of the believer who does not recite the Quran is like the date: sweet its taste, with no scent. And the example of the hypocrite who recites the Quran is like basil: sweet its scent, bitter its taste. And the example of the hypocrite who does not recite the Quran is like colocynth: bitter its taste, vile its scent."" And this hadith is only known from the hadith of Qatada, from Anas, from Abu Musa; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Awf, from Qasama, from Abu Musa, raised (marfu), except al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman."
"3029","3029 - Uqba ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us: Ribi ibn Ulayya informed us: Awf informed us, from Qasama ibn Zuhayr, from Abu Musa, raising it (to the Prophet). He said: When Adam was expelled from Paradise, he was provisioned of the fruits of Paradise, and he was taught the craft of everything; so these fruits of yours are of the fruits of Paradise, except that these change while those do not change. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Awf, from Qasama, from Abu Musa, stopped (mawquf); and we do not know anyone who raised it except Ribi."
"3030","3030 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it: Ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Awf, from Qasama, from Abu Musa, with something like it, but he did not raise it."
"3031","3031 - Amr ibn Ali, Muhammad ibn Mamar and Abd Allah ibn Ishaq informed us, saying: Abu Asim informed us: Awf informed us, from Qasama: I thought from al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""When {And warn your nearest kin} was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began calling them tribe by tribe."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this way; and we do not know Awf narrated it except Abu Asim."
"3032","3032 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Rawh ibn al-Musayyab informed us: Yazid al-Raqashi informed us, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""When Allah, blessed and exalted, created Adam (peace be upon him), He grasped from his clay two handfuls: a handful in His right and a handful in His other hand. So He said to those in His right: These are for Paradise, and I do not care. And He said to those in His other hand: These are for the Fire, and I do not care. Then He returned them into the loins of Adam, and they reproduce upon that until now."" And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from Abu Musa, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3033","3033 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us: Thabit ibn Umara informed us, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Any woman who perfumes herself so her scent is found, she is in the position of the adulteress."""
"3034","3034 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us: Ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Thabit ibn Umara, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: ""Every eye is adulterous."" And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Abu Musa; and Thabit ibn Umara is well-known: Yahya ibn Said, Ibn Abi Adi, Marwan ibn Muawiya and others narrated from him. And Ghunaym ibn Qays: al-Jurayri, Asim al-Ahwal, Thabit ibn Umara and Yazid al-Raqashi narrated from him."
"3035","3035 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Ibn Abi Adi informed us: Thabit ibn Umara informed us, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""The number of the people of Badr was the number of the companions of Talut on the day of Jalut: three hundred and seventeen."" And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Musa except from this way."
"3036","3036 - Rizq Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm informed us: Marwan ibn Muawiya informed us, from Thabit ibn Umara, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I supplicated for the Arabs, saying: O Allah, whoever of them meets You believing in You, certain, then forgive him."" And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Thabit ibn Umara except Marwan; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Marwan except al-Hasan ibn Bishr."
"3037","3037 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: al-Jurayri informed us, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The example of the heart is like a feather in a desert land, turned by the wind belly to back."" And we do not know al-Jurayri ascribed from Ghunaym, from Abu Musa, except this hadith."
"3038","3038 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid informed us: Ayyub informed us, from Abu Qilaba, and al-Qasim al-Tamimi, from Zahdam, who said: There was enmity between this tribe and the Asharis. We were with Abu Musa, when food containing chicken meat was brought to him, and with him was a man of Banu Taym Allah, red, as if of the freed slaves. So he invited him to the food, but he said: I saw it eating something, so I found it filthy, and I swore not to eat it. So he said: Come, let me narrate to you about that. I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of the Asharis, seeking mounts from him. So he said: ""By Allah, I shall not mount you, nor have I what to mount you upon."" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought camels, so he asked about us and said: ""Where are the Ashari group?"" So he ordered for us five camels with white humps. When we returned we said among ourselves: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore not to mount us, and he had not what to mount us upon, then he mounted us - so we made the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forget his oath. By Allah, we shall never prosper. So we returned to him and said: We asked you to mount us, and you swore not to mount us, then you mounted us. So he said: ""I am not the one who mounted you, but Allah mounted you. And I, by Allah, do not swear an oath and then see another better than it, except that I do what is better and release it (by expiation)."""
"3039","3039 - And Ahmad ibn Abda informed us: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3040","3040 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu al-Salil, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3041","3041 - And Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Ubulli informed us: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar informed us: Shuba informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu al-Salil, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like the hadith of Abd al-Wahhab, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Zahdam and al-Qasim al-Taymi, with something like it. And the hadith of Shuba from al-Taymi, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shuba except Badal ibn al-Muhabbar."
"3042","3042 - Yahya ibn Hakim and Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai narrated to us, saying: Abu Qutayba informed us: Imran Abu al-Awwam informed us, from Qatada, from Zahdam al-Jarmi, who said: I entered upon Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was eating chicken meat. So he said: Draw near and eat, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating chicken. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatada except Imran, nor anyone who narrated it from Imran except Abu Qutayba."
"3043","3043 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating chicken meat. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who ascribed it from Ayyub except Ibn Uyayna; while others besides Ibn Uyayna narrated it from Ayyub, stopped (mawquf)."
"3044","3044 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Sadusi informed us: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Zahdam, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it."
"3045","3045 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us: my father informed us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: ""He is not of us who shaves (the head in mourning), nor tears (clothes), nor wails."" And we do not know anyone who narrated, from Asim al-Ahwal, an ascribed hadith except this hadith; nor anyone who narrated it from Dawud except Abd al-Warith."
"3046","3046 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Awf, from Khalid al-Ahdab, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, he said: Abu Musa fell unconscious and they wept over him, so he said: I declare myself innocent before you of that from which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared himself innocent; he said: He is not of us who shaves off hair, nor tears clothes, nor wails loudly."
"3047","3047 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, informed us, from al-Hasan, from Asid ibn al-Mutashammis, he said: We went out with the Ash'aris, then we turned back and a group hastened ahead, I being among them, and we became cut off from the people. Then a slave girl came on a mule, so I brought her near a tree and helped her down, then I returned to my seat. Abu Musa said to me: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate to us? We said: Yes. He said: Before the Hour there will be harj. We said: What is harj? He said: Killing and lying. So we said to al-Ash'ari: More than what we kill today? He said: It is not your killing of the disbelievers. We fell silent and none of us uttered a clear word. He said: We said: Then what? He said: A man killing his brother. We said: And will we have our minds with us on that day? He said: No, the minds of most of your time, or most of the people of your time, will be taken away, and there will remain ignorant riffraff among the people; most of them will think they are upon something, while they are upon nothing. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I feared those days would overtake me and you, and I know no way out for me and you from them according to what our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to us, except that we exit from them as we entered them, introducing nothing new therein."
"3048","3048 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Awf, from al-Hasan, from Usayd, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"3049","3049 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: I heard Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi, from Abu Musa, with something similar, and he did not raise it to the Prophet."
"3050","3050 - Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one of this ummah hears of me, neither Jew nor Christian, then does not believe in me, except that he will be among the people of the Fire. And this wording, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Musa with this chain, and I do not think Sa'id ibn Jubayr heard from Abu Musa."
"3051","3051 - Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il informed us, from Ya'qub ibn Isma'il ibn Yasar al-Madini, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he entered a garden of the gardens of the Ansar and performed ablution, then he came until he sat on the edge of the well, then he said: O Abu Musa, guard the door for me. Then a man sought permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise; and behold it was Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. He entered and praised Allah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated him on his right. Then Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, sought permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. He entered and he seated him on his left, and the edge became full. Then Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, sought permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, upon a trial that will befall him. He entered while the edge was full, so he sat facing them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Harmalah, from Sa'id, from Abu Musa, except Ya'qub ibn Isma'il; and Sulayman ibn Bilal and Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Musa, something similar to this story."
"3052","3052 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ghassan ibn Mudar informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Maslamah informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Musa."
"3053","3053 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Isma'il ibn Imran, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa."
"3054","3054 - And Salamah ibn Shabib informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, their narrations being close together, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden in Madinah, and he covered himself with his garment, and I closed the door, I think he said, upon him. Then a man came and knocked on the door, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abd Allah ibn Qays, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I opened for him and behold it was Abu Bakr. I said: Rejoice, may Allah and His Messenger give you glad tidings; rejoice with Paradise. He entered and praised Allah and sat. Then a man came and knocked on the door, so he said: O Abd Allah, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise. So I opened for him and behold it was Umar. I said: Rejoice, may Allah and His Messenger give you glad tidings; rejoice with Paradise. He praised Allah and sat. And a man came and knocked on the door, so he said: O Abd Allah ibn Qays, open for him and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and he will meet, and he will meet. And behold it was Uthman. I said: Rejoice, may Allah and His Messenger give you glad tidings with Paradise. He praised Allah and sat, then he said: What is this word which you said to me and did not say to my two companions? And this wording is the wording of Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Maslamah."
"3055","3055 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from his father, he said: Qatadah informed us, from Abu al-Hajjaj, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A permission-seeker sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise; and behold it was Abu Bakr. Then another sought permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise; and behold it was Umar. Then another sought permission, so he said: Admit him and give him glad tidings of Paradise upon a calamity, I think he said, that will befall him; and behold it was Uthman. So Uthman said: I ask Allah for patience. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Sulayman al-Taymi, and it has been narrated through various paths from Abu Musa."
"3056","3056 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi. 3057 - And Abu Kamil informed us of it, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan, their wordings being close together, that Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, led them in prayer, and when he sat for the tashahhud, a man among the people said: You have joined prayer with righteousness and zakah. When Abu Musa turned, he said: Which of you is the one who said such-and-such words? The people fell silent. He said: Which of you is the one who said such-and-such? The people fell silent. He said: O Hittan, perhaps you said it. I said: I did not say it, and I feared you would rebuke me with it. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, and explained our sunnah to us and taught us our prayer, so he said: When you pray, straighten your rows and let one of you lead you; when he says takbir, say takbir, and when he says: Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray, say: Amin, Allah will answer you; and when he says takbir and bows, then bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is matched by that. And when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, Allah will hear you, for Allah, blessed and exalted, said upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah hears whoever praises Him. And when he says takbir and prostrates, say takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is matched by that. And when at the sitting, let the first of the words of one of you be: Greetings, good words, prayers belong to Allah; I bear witness there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."
"3057","3057 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Qatadah. 3059 - And Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam informed us of it, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar, and he added therein: And when the imam recites, be silent. A group narrated this hadith from Qatadah with this chain, and we do not know anyone who said therein: And when the imam recites, be silent, except al-Taymi, except one hadith."
"3058","3058 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated it to us, he said: Salim ibn Nuh informed us, from Umar ibn Amir, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar to the hadith of al-Taymi, as al-Taymi narrated it: And when the imam recites, be silent."
"3059","3059 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, he said: One who heard Hittan ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi narrated to me, saying: Abu Musa said: I said to a companion of mine: Come, let us dedicate this day of ours to Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard our saying, so he ascended the minbar then said: One of them says: Come, let us dedicate this day of ours to Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept repeating it until I wished I had sunk into the earth. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Musa through this path."
"3060","3060 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts perpetually, Hell will be constricted upon him like this, and he closed ninety."
"3061","3061 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Yasar informed us, he said: Abu Tamimah informed us, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts perpetually, Hell will be constricted upon him, and he closed ninety. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Qatadah, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Musa, as mawquf, and Ibn Abi Adi raised it from Ibn Abi Arubah. Its meaning in my view, and Allah knows best, is that it will be constricted upon him so he will not enter it as recompense for his fasting; and it is also possible that if he fasts the days which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting, deliberately opposing the Messenger, that would be punishment for opposing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3062","3062 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Bayan informed us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Yasar informed us, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, mighty and majestic, does not love the frequent tasters, male or female."
"3063","3063 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Bayan informed us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Tamimah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3064","3064 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Shaybah ibn Na'amah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Isa, from one who narrated to him from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Women are not divorced except out of suspicion; Allah, blessed and exalted, does not love the frequent tasters, male or female."
"3065","3065 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Amr informed us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves this world harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves the Hereafter harms his world; so harm the perishing for the lasting."
"3066","3066 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah ibn Hantab, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer. And these two hadiths, we do not know them narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3067","3067 - Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Awf informed us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Abu Kinanah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the door of a house in which there was a group of Quraysh, and he took hold of the two doorposts, then said: Is there in the house anyone but a Qurashi? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, except so-and-so, the son of our sister. He said: The son of the sister of a people is of them. Then he said (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This authority is in Quraysh as long as, when mercy is sought from them, they show mercy, and when they judge, they are just, and when they distribute, they are fair. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Musa with this chain; and Abu Kinanah, Ziyad ibn Mikhraq narrated two hadiths from him, this being one of them, and the other was raised by Abd Allah ibn Humran, while others besides Abd Allah do not raise it."
"3068","3068 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Humran informed us, he said: Awf informed us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Abu Kinanah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Part of glorifying the majesty of Allah is honoring the grey-haired Muslim, and the bearer of the Quran who is neither excessive regarding it nor neglectful of it."
"3069","3069 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, he said: Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi Abd Allah, informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, good and evil are two innate dispositions set up for people on the Day of Resurrection; as for good, it draws its people near, and as for evil, it says to its people: To me, to me. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3070","3070 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When two Muslims face one another with their swords, and one of them kills his companion, both are in the Fire. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the killer, so what of the killed? He said: He intended to kill his companion. And this hadith is only narrated from al-Taymi, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah."
"3071","3071 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah informed us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah informed us, from Ali ibn Ali al-Rifa'i, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa, he raised it, he said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, people will be presented in three presentations; as for two presentations, they are argument and excuses, and as for the third, the flying of the books to the right and to the left. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain from Abu Musa."
"3072","3072 - Umar ibn al-Khattab informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques, of light on the Day of Resurrection."
"3073","3073 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays backgammon has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"3074","3074 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Makki ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind informed us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, he said: Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people at Basra and said: O people, beware of this backgammon, playing with it, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever plays with it has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"3075","3075 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar informed us, he said: Malik informed us, from Musa ibn Maysarah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet, upon him be peace, with something similar."
"3076","3076 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray', Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, Yahya ibn Sa'id, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid, Abu Mu'awiyah, and Hammad ibn Mas'adah informed us, all of them from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, permitted the wearing of silk for the females of my ummah, and forbade it for its males."
"3077","3077 - Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi informed us, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Anas informed us, from his two grandfathers Zayd and Ziyad, they said: We came to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, and Abu Musa said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, blessed and exalted, does not accept the prayer of a man in whose body there is anything of khaluq perfume."
"3078","3078 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr informed us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi informed us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from his two grandfathers Zayd and Ziyad, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"3079","3079 - Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Baghdadi and Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim informed us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, he said: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, informed us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi', that he entered upon Abu Musa while he was being cupped at night, and he said: If only this were daytime. He said: Do you command me to shed my blood while I am fasting, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Sa'id, from Matar, from Bakr, from Abu Rafi', from Abu Musa, as mawquf."
"3080","3080 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Masruq ibn Aws, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3081","3081 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Masruq ibn Aws, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Thus Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated it from Sa'id, from Ghalib, from Masruq, from Abu Musa; and Shu'bah also narrated it from Ghalib, from Masruq, from Abu Musa, and Ibn Ulayyah followed them; and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Arubah, adding one man in the chain beyond them."
"3082","3082 - Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Ghalib al-Tammar, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Masruq ibn Aws, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and their wordings of the text of the hadith are the same, that he said: For fingers, ten each."
"3083","3083 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i informed us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Paradise is beneath the shadows of swords. A youth stood up to him and said: Did you yourself hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. So he broke the scabbard of his sword, then said to his companions: Peace be upon you, then he entered, meaning into battle."
"3084","3084 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad informed us. 3087 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali informed us, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two gardens of gold, their vessels and what is in them, and two gardens of silver, their vessels and what is in them; and between the people and seeing their Lord, blessed and exalted, there is nothing but the cloak of grandeur upon His face in the Garden of Eden. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3085","3085 - Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd Allah ibn Qays, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tent is a hollow pearl, sixty miles wide; in every corner of it are inhabitants whom the others do not see; the believer goes around among them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Musa, and we know no path for it from Abu Musa except this path."
"3086","3086 - Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, they said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"3087","3087 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah informed us, he said: al-Bakhtari ibn al-Mukhtar informed us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr and Abu Burdah narrating from their father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): This ummah is a ummah shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter; its punishment was placed in this world: killing and the like. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa except from the narration of al-Bakhtari ibn al-Mukhtar from him; and it was narrated from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from more than one angle."
"3088","3088 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Abu Yunus, and he is Hatim ibn Abi Sagheerah, from Abu Balj, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, he said: I asked Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, about the plague, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked and said: The stabbing of your enemies from the jinn, and it is martyrdom for you. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa from his father except Abu Balj."
"3089","3089 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Ajlah informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent him to Yemen, said: Forbid them every intoxicant. And we do not know Ajlah narrated with a raised chain from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa from his father except this hadith."
"3090","3090 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If a stone were thrown into Hell, it would not reach its bottom for seventy autumns. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle, and Ata ibn al-Sa'ib did not narrate from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa from his father except this hadith."
"3091","3091 - al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud informed us, he said: Badr ibn Uthman informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a questioner came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the times of prayer, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer anything. Then he commanded Bilal, and he called the adhan for Fajr when dawn split, and he prayed. Then he commanded him and he called the adhan for Zuhr when the sun declined, while one saying said: It has not declined, though he knew better, and he prayed Zuhr. Then he commanded Bilal, and he stood and called the adhan for Asr when the shadow of everything became its like; and he commanded Bilal and he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun set or fell; then he commanded Bilal and he established Isha at the disappearance of the twilight; then he commanded Bilal and he established Fajr while one saying said: The sun has risen, though he, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), knew better, and he prayed Fajr. Then he commanded Bilal and he stood for Zuhr at the time of yesterday's Asr, and he prayed Asr while one saying said: The sun has reddened or has not reddened, though he knew better; and he prayed Maghrib before the twilight disappeared, and he prayed Isha up to a third of the night. Then he said: Where is the questioner about the time of prayer? What is between these two is time. And the hadith of Abu Musa, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Bakr except Badr ibn Uthman; and most of the hadiths narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) state that he prayed Maghrib on both days at one time, except this hadith of Abu Musa, and the hadith of Abu Hurayrah which al-A'mash narrated from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah, and I was told: Qatadah from Abu Ayyub from Abd Allah ibn Amr; for these narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned two times for Maghrib."
"3092","3092 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab and Mu'adh ibn Hani informed us, they said: Hammam informed us, from Abu Jamrah, from Abu Bakr, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the two cool prayers will enter Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle; it is only known from Abu Bakr ibn Umarah ibn Ruwaybah, but thus Hammam said it."
"3093","3093 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Abu Talib went out to Syria, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out with him among elders of Quraysh. When they overlooked the monk, they dismounted and left behind their mounts. The monk came out to them, though before that they would pass by him and he would not come out to them nor turn to any of them. He came weaving through them until he took the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This is the master of the worlds; this is the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds; this is the one Allah sent as mercy to the worlds. The elders of Quraysh said to him: What is your knowledge? He said: When you overlooked from the mountain pass, no tree or stone remained except it prostrated, and that prostrates only to a prophet; and I recognize him by the seal of prophethood below the cartilage of his shoulder, like an apple. Then he returned and made food for them. When he brought it to them he said: Send for him, and he was pasturing camels. He came while a cloud shaded him. When he drew near the people, he found they had preceded him to the shade of the tree. When he sat, the shade of the tree leaned over him. He said: Look how the shade of the tree leaned over him. While he stood over him, adjuring them not to take him to Rome, for if Rome saw him they would recognize him by the description and kill him, he turned and behold nine horsemen approaching from Rome. He met them and said: What brought you? They said: We came for this Prophet who is emerging in this month; no road remains but men were sent to it, and we were informed of his news so we were sent to this road of yours. He said to them: Have you left behind anyone better than you? They said: We were only chosen as the best for this road of yours. He said: Do you see, if Allah, blessed and exalted, intends to decree a matter, can anyone among people repel it? They said: No. He said: Then return. So they followed him and returned. Then he turned to these and said: I adjure you by Allah, which of you is his guardian? They said: Abu Talib. He kept adjuring him to send him back, until Abu Talib sent him back, and he sent with him one who ... Abu Bakr said: And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa from his father except Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, nor from Yunus except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan, known as Qurad."
"3094","3094 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, informed us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa."
"3095","3095 - And Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa informed us, he said: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, informed us, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from his father Abu Musa, and the wording is that of Amr ibn Ali, that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over an animal, neither having proof, so he judged it between them in halves."
"3096","3096 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh informed us, he said: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah is a ummah shown mercy; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter; its punishment is in this world: earthquakes and killing."
"3097","3097 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Charity is due upon every Muslim. They said: And whoever does not find? He said: He works with his hand and benefits himself. They said: And whoever does not find? He said: He helps the one in need, the distressed; he enjoins good and forbids evil and withholds from evil, and that is charity. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who raised it with a chain from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah except Shu'bah."
"3098","3098 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Samurah informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Juhadah informed us, from Musa al-Juhani, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: On the Day of Resurrection, every man will take the hand of a man from the people of polytheism, and it will be said: O Muslim, or O believer, this is your ransom from the Fire. And we do not know Musa al-Juhani narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah from his father from Abu Musa except this hadith."
"3099","3099 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari and Ubadah ibn Abd Allah al-Qasmali informed us, they said: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi informed us, he said: Mujammi' informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we said: If only we sat until we pray Isha with him. So we sat, and he came out to us and said: You have remained here? We said: Yes, we prayed Maghrib, then we said: We will pray Isha with you. He said: You did well. And he raised his head to the sky, and he would often raise his head to the sky, and said: The stars are a security for the people of heaven; when the stars go, there comes to the people of heaven what they are promised. And I am a security for my companions; when I go, there comes to my companions what they are promised. And my companions are a security for my ummah; when my companions go, there comes to my ummah what they are promised. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Musa, and we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3100","3100 - Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Nafi' informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, he said: Whenever I heard a hadith I would write it down, so my father said to me: O my son, what are you doing? I said: I write down what I hear from you. He said: Then bring it to me. So I read it to him, and he said: Yes, thus I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); but I fear you may add or omit."
"3101","3101 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah informed us, from his father, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A drink called bit' made of honey, and mizr made of barley. He said: Do they both intoxicate? They said: Yes. He said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"3102","3102 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3103","3103 - And Yahya ibn Hakim informed us of it, he said: Uthman ibn Umar and Abu Qutaybah informed us, they said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. Thus Isra'il narrated it."
"3104","3104 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not mention Abu Musa. Abu Bakr said: Bishr ibn Mansur and Ja'far ibn Awn raised it with a connected chain."
"3105","3105 - Abu Kamil al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn informed us, he said: Bishr ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. And Abu Bakr said: Bishr was among the most virtuous of creation."
"3106","3106 - Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"3107","3107 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not say from Abu Musa."
"3108","3108 - And Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi and Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Jazari informed us, they said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, thus they both said: From Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"3109","3109 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj informed us, he said: Talq ibn Ghannam informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3110","3110 - And Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt informed us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3111","3111 - And Ruzayq ibn al-Sakht informed us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, from his father, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3112","3112 - And Abu Kamil informed us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3113","3113 - And Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik informed us, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. Abu Bakr said: The hadith belongs to the one who adds when he is a preserver, and Isra'il is a preserver from Abu Ishaq; and those who narrated it from Shu'bah and al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian; those who said: From Abu Burdah from Abu Musa have brought what Shu'bah and al-Thawri brought, and Isra'il is not rejected regarding the hadith of Abu Ishaq and his preservation of it. Abu Bakr said: It only reached me that al-Thawri and Shu'bah said to Abu Ishaq: Did Abu Burdah narrate to you from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; and it did not reach us that they said: Did Abu Burdah narrate to you? So he said: No; rather Abu Burdah narrated it to me; though Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq is trustworthy, and Sharik and Qays followed Isra'il in his chain and connection; and Bishr ibn Mansur, and he was among the best of people, raised it with a connected chain from Sufyan; and Ja'far ibn Awn also raised it with a connected chain from Sufyan. And we do not know, among what Ja'far ibn Awn narrated, hadiths counted against him as errors in which this would be counted as his error; so the hadith in our view has continuous reports in its connection and raising, and if one who falls short falls short with it, the report is established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3114","3114 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is with men who play with the limits of Allah; one of them says: I have divorced you, I have taken you back, meaning to his wife. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who raised it with a connected chain from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, except al-Thawri; and Mu'ammal and Abu Hudhayfah narrated it from al-Thawri."
"3115","3115 - Khallad ibn Aslam al-Marwazi informed us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The orphan girl is consulted regarding herself; if she is silent, she has permitted, and if she dislikes, there is no compulsion upon her nor binding over her."
"3116","3116 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Yemen, saying: Give glad tidings and do not repel, and make easy and do not make difficult. Mu'adh said: You are sending us to a land of many drinks, so what shall we drink? He said: Drink, but do not drink an intoxicant."
"3117","3117 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Mughirah, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: There was sharpness in my tongue toward my family, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I feared my tongue would admit me to the Fire. He said: Then where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from Allah a hundred times a day. Abu Ishaq said: So I narrated it to Abu Burdah, and he narrated it to me from his father, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I seek forgiveness from Allah a hundred times a day. And the hadith of Abu Ishaq from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa, I heard it only from Nasr from Abu Ahmad."
"3118","3118 - Yahya ibn Khalaf Abu Salamah informed us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None of you will be saved by his deed. It was said: Not even you? He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with mercy from Him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Ishaq from Abu Burdah except Ash'ath ibn Sawwar."
"3119","3119 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi informed us, he said: Uthman ibn Sa'id ibn Murrah informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sent a detachment, would say: Go forth in the name of Allah and fight whoever disbelieves in Allah; do not steal spoils, do not mutilate, and do not kill an infant. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa from the Prophet, upon him be peace, except with this chain from this angle."
"3120","3120 - Salih ibn Mu'adh Abu Bishr informed us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah informed us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abi al-Hurr informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I seek forgiveness from Allah a hundred times a day. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah from his father from Abu Musa except al-Mughirah ibn Abi al-Hurr."
"3121","3121 - Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Abu Badr Shuja' ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Ziyad ibn Khaythamah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Darim, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burdah, from his father, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have grown heavy, so when I bow, bow, and when I rise, rise, and when I prostrate, prostrate; and let me not find any of you preceding me to bowing or to prostration. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain, and none narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Ziyad ibn Khaythamah."
"3122","3122 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Kathir informed us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani informed us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abu Burdah, he said: I was with Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, when a daughter of his, or a son of his, sneezed; he said tashmit to the girl and did not say it to the boy. Her mother said: Why did you say it to her and not to her brother? He said: She remembered Allah so I remembered Him for her, and he forgot Allah so I forgot him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever sneezes and praises Allah, say tashmit to him; and whoever does not praise Allah, do not say it to him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3123","3123 - Muhammad ibn Thawwab informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Hani informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, and from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not recite the Quran while you are junub, nor while you are bowing, nor while you are prostrating, nor while you are squatting like the squatting of a dog; do not pray while you have your hair tied up; do not spread your forearms like the spreading of a beast; do not wear qassi garments; do not wear a gold ring, and do not wear your ring on these two, meaning the forefinger and the middle finger. And this hadith is only known from Ali ibn Abi Talib, but this man combined Abu Musa with Ali in it, and we do not know anyone who combined them except Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn, and he was not followed in it."
"3124","3124 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, that Umar ibn al-Khattab met Asma bint Umays and said: O Abyssinian woman, you are a fine people, were it not for our precedence over you in migration; so we are better than you. She said: By Allah, I will enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him of what you said, O son of al-Khattab. So she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather, you have two migrations: your migration to the land of Abyssinia, and your migration to here. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa with this wording except Adi ibn Thabit, and we do not know Adi narrated with a raised chain from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except this hadith."
"3125","3125 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari informed us, he said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim informed us, he said: Shayban, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, informed us, from al-Ash'ath ibn Abi al-Sha'tha, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to wear wool and ride a goat bareback. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle; and some of the companions of Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated it from Hashim, from Shayban, from Ash'ath, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as mursal; and Bishr ibn Khalid raised it with a connected chain for us, saying: From Abu Burdah from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3126","3126 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: al-Harish ibn Sulaym informed us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. And we do not know Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Talhah except al-Harish ibn Sulaym."
"3127","3127 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Qurrah informed us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa."
"3128","3128 - And Yahya informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman informed us, he said: Qurrah ibn Khalid informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two men of the Ash'aris, one on my right and the other on my left, while the Messenger of Allah, upon him be peace, was using the tooth-stick. Both of them asked for office. He said: O Abu Musa, or O Abd Allah ibn Qays, we do not appoint over our work one who seeks it. I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, they did not inform me of what was in themselves, and I did not know they sought office; and it is as if I look at his tooth-stick beneath his lip. He said: Go, you O Abu Musa, or O Abd Allah ibn Qays. So he sent him to Yemen, then he sent Mu'adh ibn Jabal. When he arrived, he cast a cushion for him and said: Alight; and behold a man with him, bound. He said: What is this? He said: This was a Jew who embraced Islam, then returned to his religion, the evil religion, becoming Jewish again. He said: I will not alight until he is killed. So he commanded regarding him and he was killed. Then they discussed standing at night; Mu'adh said: As for me, I stand and sleep, and I hope in my sleep what I hope in my standing."
"3129","3129 - And al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn informed us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan informed us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he sent him and Mu'adh to Yemen, and he mentioned this story and narrated something similar to the hadith of Qurrah."
"3130","3130 - Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i informed us, he said: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shu'ayb informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that he sought permission upon Umar three times and was not permitted, as he was busy. When he finished he said: Did I not hear Abd Allah ibn Qays, or the voice of Abd Allah ibn Qays? Admit him. It was said: He went back. He said: Call him. He came and said: We were commanded with that. He said to us: Bring me proof of that. So he brought Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who testified for him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking permission is three times."
"3131","3131 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Rabi' informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah informed us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: If you had seen us while we were with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and rain befell us, you would have thought, or you would indeed have thought, our smell was the smell of sheep. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of Qatadah from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sulayman from Humayd from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except Abd Allah ibn al-Rabi'."
"3132","3132 - Abu Kamil informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: If you had seen us with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and rain befell us, you would have thought our smell was the smell of sheep."
"3133","3133 - And Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he feared a people, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from their evils, and I place You before them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except Qatadah."
"3134","3134 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, informed us, from Hammam, from Matar, from Qatadah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Hammam, from Matar, from Qatadah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi."
"3135","3135 - Musa ibn Sufyan informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Jahm informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and sent Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Yemen, saying: Make easy and do not make difficult, give glad tidings and do not repel. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Sha'bi from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except Ibn Abi Layla, nor did anyone narrate it from Ibn Abi Layla except Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"3136","3136 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj informed us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn Abu Nu'aym informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Qays informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Sa'd fell ill at Makkah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to visit him and said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you not dislike that a man die in the land from which he migrated? He said: Yes; and perhaps Allah, blessed and exalted, will raise you so He harms a people through you and benefits others through you. And this hadith was narrated by others besides Muhammad ibn Umar, mentioning it from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Qays from Abu Burdah as mursal; and Muhammad ibn Umar was trustworthy."
"3137","3137 - Muhammad ibn Umar informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il informed us, from Tulayq ibn Imran, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever separates a parent from his child. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa from the Prophet, upon him be peace, except with this chain; and others besides Ibrahim ibn Isma'il narrated it from Tulayq ibn Imran ibn Husayn as mursal."
"3138","3138 - Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with two men of the Ash'aris, and they asked him for office. The Messenger of Allah, upon him be peace, said: We do not appoint over our work one who is eager for it or one who seeks it."
"3139","3139 - Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Shaddad ibn Sa'id informed us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Burdah, he said: My father said to me: Do you hear from me? I said: Yes. He said: Then bring it to me. I said: I write it down. He said: Then bring it to me. So I brought it to him and he erased it, then said: Memorize as we memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ghaylan from Abu Burdah except Shaddad ibn Sa'id; and Khalid ibn Salamah narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa, and he did not raise it."
"3140","3140 - Nasr ibn Ali informed us of it, he said: Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' informed us, from Khalid ibn Salamah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, with something similar, and he did not raise it."
"3141","3141 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi informed us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Marwan informed us, he said: Ghaylan ibn Jarir informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; some of us fasting and some of us breaking fast, and neither did the fasting criticize the breaking nor the breaking criticize the fasting. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ghaylan except al-Walid ibn Marwan."
"3142","3142 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Hakim ibn al-Daylam, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Jews would sneeze before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), hoping he would say: May Allah have mercy on you; but he would say: May Allah guide you. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3143","3143 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, from Yunus ibn al-Harith, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah praying upon his mount, here and here and here, to his right and to his left and before him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain."
"3144","3144 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid informed us, from Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a funeral passed by him, its people hastening with it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is moderation in your funerals. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Layth, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, and we know for it only this path."
"3145","3145 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi informed us, from Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer, then said: O people, Allah commanded you to fear Allah and to speak a right word. Then he passed through the men to the women and said: Allah commands me to command you to fear Allah and to speak a right word."
"3146","3146 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the matter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us, we went out to Abyssinia, until our ship cast us to the Negus in Abyssinia; and we met Ja'far ibn Abi Talib while he was with the Negus. Ja'far said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us here and commanded us to stay, so we stayed with him until we all came together."
"3147","3147 - Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Mukhawwal ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, you send me to Yemen, where there are the drinks bit' and mizr. He said: I do not know what these names are; I forbid for you every intoxicant. And we do not know Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis narrated from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except this hadith."
"3148","3148 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj informed us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Yemen, saying: Make easy and do not make difficult, give glad tidings and do not repel, and do not disobey one another. Mu'adh said: We come to a land in which drinks are many. He said: Drink, but do not drink an intoxicant."
"3149","3149 - Ali ibn Mu'attib informed us, he said: Ali ibn Asim informed us, he said: Asim ibn Kulayb informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"3150","3150 - al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami informed us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Jamil informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me and Mu'adh ibn Jabal to Yemen, appointing each of us over a district, saying: Make easy and do not make difficult, give glad tidings and do not repel. Each of them went to his work; whenever one of them needed something from his companion, he would come to him, greet him, and renew the bond with him. Mu'adh drew near Abu Musa, coming riding on his mule until he stood over him, and behold with him was a man whose hand was bound to his neck. He said to Abu Musa: What is this? He said: This is a man who apostatized from Islam, or disbelieved after his Islam. He said: I will not dismount until he is killed. So he was killed, then he dismounted."
"3151","3151 - And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi' informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"3152","3152 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Any man who has a slave girl, and he disciplines her and disciplines her well and teaches her, then frees her and marries her, he has two rewards. And we do not know al-Fadl ibn Yazid narrated with a raised chain from al-Sha'bi from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except this hadith."
"3153","3153 - And Fadalh ibn al-Fadl informed us of it, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash informed us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"3154","3154 - And Salamah ibn Shabib informed us of it, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' informed us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer, he has no prayer, I think he said, except with an excuse. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Abu Husayn, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, as mawquf."
"3155","3155 - And Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli informed us of it, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay' informed us, from Simak, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Whoever hears the call and does not answer, he has no prayer. And we do not know Simak narrated from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Simak except Hafs."
"3156","3156 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Talhah ibn Yahya, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Makkah, with my two brothers Abu Amir ibn Qays and Abu Burdah ibn Qays, and five of the Ash'aris, until we came to Madinah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: People have one migration, and you have two migrations. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Talhah with this chain except Abu Usamah."
"3157","3157 - Abd Allah ibn Ja'far al-Barmaki informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi informed us, he said: Talhah ibn Yahya narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you had seen me last night while I listened to your recitation, you have been given of the flutes of the family of Dawud. He said: I said: Had I known you were listening to my recitation, I would have beautified it for you. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Talhah from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi."
"3158","3158 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from his brother, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Two men of the Ash'aris came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), hinting at office, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most treacherous of you in my view is whoever seeks it; so he did not employ them in anything. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Isma'il, with this chain, and we do not know with this chain except this hadith."
"3159","3159 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis informed us, he said: Musa ibn Dawud informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"3160","3160 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari and Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Qasmali informed us, they said: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Burqan informed us, from Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over land belonging to one of them in Hadramawt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the defendant: Do you swear by Allah besides whom there is no god? The claimant said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing but his oath; then he will take my land. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he swears falsely, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify him, and for him is a painful punishment. The man refrained from it, so he returned it to him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle, and Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj did not narrate from Abu Burdah except this hadith."
"3161","3161 - Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn al-Hakam ibn Jahl informed us, he said: Umar al-Abahh, and he is Umar ibn Sa'id, informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from al-Hakam ibn Jahl, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has not concealed a sin of a servant in this world and then shames him with it on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Musa with this chain, and we heard it only from Nasr ibn Ali."
"3162","3162 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burdah, from his grandfather Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked one day, and when they pressed him much, he became angry, then said to the people: Ask me whatever you wish. A man stood and said: Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your father is Salim, the freed slave of Shaybah. Another man stood and said: Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. When Umar saw what was on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of anger, he said: O Messenger of Allah, we repent to Allah; we are pleased with Allah as Lord and with you as Messenger. So it was lifted from him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3163","3163 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greatest of people in reward for prayer are the farthest of them in walking to it; and the one who waits for prayer until he prays it with the imam in congregation is greater in reward than the one who prays it then sleeps. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3164","3164 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A house burned down in Madinah upon its people at night. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of their affair, he came to them and said: This fire is an enemy to you; when you sleep, extinguish it; or he said: This fire is an enemy to you; when you sleep, extinguish it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3165","3165 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You will come to the Hawd and be snatched away from me; so I will say: O Lord, my companions, O Lord, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. So I will say: Away, away. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3166","3166 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd ibn Abd Allah, from his grandfather Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The parable of what Allah sent me with of knowledge and guidance is like rain that fell upon land; part of it accepted the water and grew abundant grass and herbage; and part of it held the water, so Allah benefits people through it, and they drank and pastured and watered; and another part of it the water struck, which is only barren flats that hold no water and grow no herbage. Such is the parable of whoever understood the religion of Allah and benefited from what Allah sent me with, learning and teaching; and the parable of whoever did not lift his head with that and did not accept the guidance of Allah with which I was sent. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3167","3167 - Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which Muslims are best? He said: The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."
"3168","3168 - And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us of it, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to me, he said: Burayd narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith is only known from the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id from Burayd; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Usamah from Burayd except Ibrahim ibn Sa'id."
"3169","3169 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Burayd narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood frightened, fearing it was the Hour, until he came to the mosque. He stood and prayed with the longest standing, bowing, and prostration, then said: These signs which Allah sends are not for the death of anyone nor his life; but Allah sends them to frighten His servants. When you see anything of them, rush to His remembrance, His supplication, and His forgiveness. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle."
"3170","3170 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Burayd narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him. And this hadith, we know no path for it from Abu Musa except this path."
"3171","3171 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id and Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari informed us, they said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle."
"3172","3172 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"3173","3173 - And Abu al-Sa'ib Salm ibn Junadah ibn Salm informed us of it, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from this angle; and more than one narrated it from Abu Usamah, and the hadith is known through Abu Kurayb."
"3174","3174 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends mercy for an ummah, He takes its prophet before it, and makes him a forerunner and predecessor for it; and when Allah intends the destruction of an ummah, He punishes it while its prophet is alive, destroying it while he watches. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Musa with this chain."
"3175","3175 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I and my companions of the people of the ship intended to meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Madinah, while they were staying at Baqi' Duhnan. We would take turns visiting the Messenger of Allah, upon him be peace, at Isha prayer every night. He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions while he was occupied with some of his affair, until he delayed Isha until the night grew dark. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and prayed with them. When he finished his prayer he said: Wait; rejoice, for among the blessing of Allah upon you is that none among people prays this prayer but you; or he said: None prayed this prayer but you. So we returned at the time we heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3176","3176 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon people a time when a man circles with charity of gold and finds none who takes it from him; and one man will be followed by, or will stand for, a hundred women, or forty women, due to the fewness of men and the multitude of women. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"3177","3177 - Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami informed us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, informed us, from Abu Burdah, and he is Burayd ibn Abd Allah, from his grandfather Abu Burdah ibn Abi Musa, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Intercede and you will be rewarded; and Allah decrees upon the tongue of His Prophet what He wills, or what He loves; and the trustworthy treasurer who gives what he is commanded, his soul content with it, is one of the givers of charity."
"3178","3178 - And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us of it, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when a questioner came to him he would say: Intercede and you will be rewarded; and Allah decrees upon the tongue of His Prophet what He wills. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The trustworthy treasurer who gives what he is commanded, his soul content with it, is one of the givers of charity. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Musa except from the hadith of Burayd from Abu Burdah from him."
"3179","3179 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"3180","3180 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Hamdani informed us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, from Burayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Burdah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah gives respite to the wrongdoer; when He seizes him, He does not let him go. Then he recited: And thus is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are wrongdoing; His seizure is painful, severe."
"3181","3181 - And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us, Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. Abu Bakr said: And this hadith is only known through Abu Mu'awiyah from Burayd; and we knew no one who narrated it besides Abu Mu'awiyah, until Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us of it from Abu Usamah; and we did not see it with anyone from Abu Usamah except with Ibrahim; and the hearing of Ibrahim ibn Sa'id from Abu Usamah, and the hearing of al-Mu'ayti, is one; and it reached me that he followed Ibrahim in this hadith."
"3182","3182 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub and Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi informed us, they said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himmani informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He was given of the flutes of the family of Dawud. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Burayd from Abu Burdah from Abu Musa except Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani."
"3183","3183 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Burayd narrated to me, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh ibn Jabal and Abu Musa to Yemen, saying: Give glad tidings and do not repel, and make easy and do not make difficult."
"3184","3184 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the conquest of Khaybar, and he gave us a share, and he gave no share to anyone who had not witnessed it besides us."
"3185","3185 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep reciting the Quran, for it escapes from the breasts of men more swiftly than camels from their hobbles."
"3186","3186 - Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The orphan girl is consulted regarding herself; if she is silent, she has permitted, and if she dislikes, there is no compulsion upon her."
"3187","3187 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi informed us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Asim al-Ahwal informed us, from Abu Kabshah, he said: I heard Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, upon the minbar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the righteous companion is like the perfumer; even if he does not give you of his perfume, its scent reaches you. And the parable of the evil companion is like the blacksmith; even if it does not strike your clothes, its smell clings to you. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart is only named from its turning; and the parable of the heart is like a feather in a desert turned at the root of a tree, the wind turning it back and belly. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be tribulations like pieces of the dark night; a man will be a believer in the morning therein and a disbeliever in the evening. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be a tribulation in which the sitter is better than the stander, and the stander therein is better than the walker. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim from Abu Kabshah from Abu Musa except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad."
"3188","3188 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: al-Awza'i informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Musa informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, he said: Abu Musa came to the Messenger of Allah, upon him be peace."
"3189","3189 - And Azhar ibn Jamil informed us of it, he said: Yahya informed us, from al-Awza'i, from Muhammad ibn Abi Musa, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, that he brought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nabidh of a jar, fermenting; so he said: Strike it against the wall, for whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day does not drink it. Abu Bakr said: Thus Yahya narrated it from al-Awza'i."
"3190","3190 - And Hawtharah ibn Muhammad al-Minqari informed us of it, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Awza'i, from Muhammad ibn Abi Musa, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Mu'adh; and we do not know Qatadah narrated from al-Awza'i a supported hadith except this hadith."
"3191","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Kathir informed us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Iyad al-Ashari, that Abu Musa fell ill until he lost consciousness, and his wife wailed over him, so he said to her: Do you not know what I told you, and when he died we asked her: What did he say to you? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not from us who shaves, or tears, or wails loudly."
"3192","Al-Hasan ibn Qazaah informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr informed us, he said: Abu Layla informed us — Abu Bakr said: And I once heard him say: Husayn informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, and the correct version is Abu Layla — from Mazidah ibn Jabir, from his father, from Abu Musa al-Ashari (may Allah be pleased with him), that he ordered fasting Ashura, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast it."
"3193","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Isa, a man from the people of Yemen, informed us, from Salamah ibn Wahram, from a man, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The pilgrim intercedes for four hundred of his household, or he said: of the people of his house, and he comes out of his sins like the day his mother bore him."
"3194","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Hani ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar informed us, from Abu Ishaq al-Kufi, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays twelve rakahs in a day and night besides the obligatory prayer, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. Abu Bakr said: And this Abu Ishaq is Harun Abu Ishaq; Hammad ibn Zayd named him."
"3195","Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us of it, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Harun Abu Ishaq informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, except Harun, and I do not know anyone who followed Harun in this hadith, nor do I know anyone who narrated from him except these two men."
"3196","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Said informed us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Al-Walid ibn Uqbah Abu Wahb informed us, he said: Abu Burdah informed us, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, the Jews and Christians will be brought, and it will be said: This is your ransom from the Fire, O Muslim — meaning: a man of them will be handed over to every man of them."
"3197","And Abu Kurayb informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi al-Wasim informed us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3198","Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Thabit ibn Aws, or Thabit ibn Qays, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), that he lost consciousness and his wife wept, and when he recovered he said: Has what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said not reached you? He said: So I asked her, and he said: He is not from us who shaves, and wails loudly, and tears. Abu Bakr said: I heard one who mentions that shaving means scratching the face. End of the hadith of Abu Musa."
"3199","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Ayyub and Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah — one of them said: from Aishah — she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take revenge for himself for a wrong done to him at all."
"3200","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, he said: Malik informed us, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a wrong owed to his brother with him, let him come to him and seek his absolution before it is taken when there is no dinar nor dirham; if he has good deeds, they will be taken from his good deeds, and if not, they will be taken from his evil deeds and placed upon his evil deeds."
"3201","Ahmad ibn Yazdad al-Kufi informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar informed us, he said: Al-Amash informed us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is surrounded by hardships, and the Fire is surrounded by desires. And this hadith was narrated by others than Amr from al-Amash from Abu Salih in mursal form, and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Thabit from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3202","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe blood from his face on the day of Uhud and shake it off like this, and say: How can a people succeed who wounded their Prophet and broke his incisor while he calls them to Allah. Then Allah revealed: Not for you is the decision at all — the verse."
"3203","Hudbah ibn Khalid informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was frightened in Allah when no one was frightened, and I was harmed in Allah when no one was harmed, and there came upon me thirty nights when neither I nor my family had food for one with a liver to eat except something that the armpit of Bilal concealed. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit from Anas."
"3204","Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra informed us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Amr, meaning al-Fuqaymi, informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3205","And al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq informed us, he said: Israil informed us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The believer is not a stabber, nor a curser, nor obscene, nor foul-mouthed. And the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad: we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except al-Hasan ibn Amr; and the hadith of al-Amash from Ibrahim: we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash except Israil, and none narrated it from Israil in connected form except Muhammad ibn Sabiq."
"3206","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata informed us, he said: Said ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Hakim ibn Hizam (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with his Companions, he said to them: Do you hear what I hear? They said: We do not hear anything. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heaven creaked, and it is not blamed for creaking; there is not in it a handspan of space except upon it an angel prostrating or standing. Abu Bakr said: And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from the hadith of Hakim ibn Hizam from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Said from Qatadah except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata."
"3207","Ismail ibn Yaqub ibn Subayh informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Ishaq ibn Rashid informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his father, he said: Usayd ibn Hudayr had a fine voice with the Quran, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: While I was reciting on the roof of my house, with the woman in the chamber and the horse tied at the door of the chamber, there covered me something like a cloud, and I feared the horse would bolt and the woman would panic and fall, so I stopped. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite, O Usayd; that was an angel listening to the Quran. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Kab ibn Malik from his father except by this chain."
"3208","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi informed us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: I heard Abu Imran al-Jawni say regarding the saying of Allah: And the retaining ear retains it: It is an ear that understood from Allah, mighty and exalted."
"3209","Abbad ibn Ziyad al-Saji informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, from Abu Rawq, from al-Dahhak, regarding: That he may warn whoever is alive: He said: One who has sense. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Abu Muawiyah."
"3210","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal, from Qays ibn Sakan, from Abdullah, he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, originates the clouds, then sends the wind, and it gathers the clouds, and they pour forth as the milch camel pours forth. And he recited: Is it you who sent it down from the rain-clouds, or are We the senders. And this hadith is an elevated hadith with a fine chain."
"3211","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulayman informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding: Then for themselves they prepare: He said: In the grave."
"3212","Musnad of al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with them both). Musnad of al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Basri al-Bazzar informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: I warn you of the Fire, I warn you of the Fire. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3213","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar informed us, they said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to straighten the row until he made it like the arrow or the spear, then he saw a man standing apart, so he said: You shall straighten your rows, or Allah shall set your faces against one another."
"3214","And Jafar ibn Awn, nephew of Waki, informed us of it, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr informed us, he said: Misar informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3215","Fahm ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us of it, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr informed us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of the hadith of Shubah. And we do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by the narration of al-Numan ibn Bashir from him."
"3216","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: My father informed us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is the likeness of the body; when part of it aches, the rest of it responds. And the like of these words was narrated from al-Numan ibn Bashir by various routes; we shall mention each hadith of them with its wording in its place, if Allah wills."
"3217","Ali ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: My father informed us, from al-Muafa ibn Imran, from al-Mufaddal ibn Sadaqah, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: When we prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, none of us would bend his back until he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate. And we do not know this hadith narrated from al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route with this chain."
"3218","Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi informed us, he said: Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of the servant than a man with his mount in a desert land, upon it his provision and food; he came to the root of a tree and pillowed the foreleg of his she-camel, then he stood and woke to find his she-camel gone; he came to an elevation and climbed it and did not see her, then he came to another elevation until he did that repeatedly, then he said: I shall return to the place I was in until I die; so he returned, and there was his mount dragging its bridle, upon it his provision; so Allah is more intensely joyful at the repentance of the servant than that man was at his mount. And we do not know anyone who transmitted it in marfu form from Hammad ibn Salamah from Simak from al-Numan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl; others narrate it in mawquf form; and Sharik narrated it from Simak from al-Numan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3219","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3220","Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi informed us, he said: Zaidah informed us, from Simak, meaning Ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The likeness of the warrior in the path of Allah is the likeness of the fasting one standing in prayer until he returns to his house."
"3221","Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us of it, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay informed us, he said: Simak informed us, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, and he did not trace it in marfu form; and we do not know anyone who traced this hadith in marfu form from Simak from al-Numan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Husayn ibn Ali from Zaidah; others narrate it in mawquf form."
"3222","Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabubah al-Marwazi informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak from al-Numan except Husayn ibn Waqid."
"3223","Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Marwazi informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a milch animal, or guides through an alley, it is charity for him. And we do not know it narrated from al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Husayn ibn Waqid."
"3224","Salih ibn Muadh Abu Bishr informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas informed us, he said: Ayyub ibn Jabir informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the Fire even with half a date. And we do not know it narrated from al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route; and I think Ayyub ibn Jabir erred in this hadith, because Shubah and Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated this hadith from Simak ibn Harb from Abbad ibn Hubaysh from Adi ibn Hatim, and that is correct in my view."
"3225","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi informed us, he said: Aswad ibn Amir informed us, he said: Israil informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right. And this hadith was only narrated by Simak from al-Numan ibn Salim from Amr ibn Aws from his father — and they said: from Simak from al-Numan ibn Salim from Aws ibn Abi Aws — and I think Aswad ibn Amir erred in its chain."
"3226","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Ahwazi informed us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3227","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik and Hilal ibn Yahya informed us of it, they said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3228","And Ahmad ibn Aban informed us of it, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from his father, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite in the Eid prayer: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming. Habib ibn Salim added in his hadith: And he recites in Jumuah: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming; and sometimes Jumuah and Eid would fall together on the same day, and he would recite them in both together."
"3229","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith was narrated by Shubah and others, who followed Abu Awanah and Ibn Uyaynah, so we sufficed with the hadith of Abu Awanah and Ibn Uyaynah."
"3230","Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti and Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti informed us, they said: Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Abu Bishr, from Bashir ibn Thabit, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I know you best about the time of this prayer, meaning Isha; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray it at the setting of the moon on the third night. And we do not know Bashir ibn Thabit narrated from by anyone except Abu Bishr, this hadith."
"3231","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3232","And Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3233","And Yusuf ibn Musa and Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti informed us, they said: Abu Usamah informed us, from al-Amash, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man with sandals in the soles of his feet from which his brain boils. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Amash from Abu Ishaq except Abu Usamah; and the hadith of Abd al-Samad in our view is a mistake: Abd al-Samad erred in it when he made it from Shubah from Simak from al-Numan, and the correct version is what Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated from Shubah from Abu Ishaq from al-Numan; and we do not know Abu Ishaq narrated from al-Numan ibn Bashir except this hadith."
"3234","Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman informed us, he said: Musa ibn Muslim informed us, he said: Awn ibn Abdullah informed us, from his brother, or from his father, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What you mention of the majesty of Allah, blessed and exalted, of glorification and magnification and declaring oneness, they circle around the Throne with a humming like the humming of bees, mentioning their owner; does not one of you love that there ever remain with Allah one who mentions him thereby. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except by this route with this chain; and Musa ibn Muslim was narrated from by Yahya ibn Said and Abu Bahr and others."
"3235","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Al-Rabi ibn Nafi informed us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Sallam informed us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, he said: Abu Sallam narrated to me, he said: Al-Numan ibn Bashir narrated to me. [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3236","And Muhammad ibn Miskin informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan informed us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Sallam informed us, from Zayd ibn Sallam, he said: Abu Sallam narrated to me, he said: Al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, he said: I was at the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a Friday, and a man said: I do not care not to do any deed after Islam except watering the pilgrims; and another said: I do not care not to do any deed after Islam except maintaining the Sacred Mosque; and another said: Striving in the path of Allah is better than what you said; so Umar rebuked them and said: Do not raise your voices at the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a Friday; but when I pray Jumuah I shall enter upon him and ask him about what you differed over; so he entered upon him and asked him, and Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed: Did you make watering the pilgrims and maintaining the Sacred Mosque like one who believed in Allah and the Last Day and strove in the path of Allah? They are not equal with Allah, and Allah does not guide the wrongdoing people. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from al-Numan ibn Bashir by this route; and Muawiyah ibn Sallam and Zayd and Abu Sallam are well known for transmitting hadith."
"3237","Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal informed us, he said: Aban informed us, from Qatadah, from Khalid ibn Urfutah, from Habib ibn Salim, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man called Abd al-Rahman lay with his wife's slave-girl, and he was brought to al-Numan ibn Bashir, who said: I shall judge in your case by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): if she had made her lawful to you I shall flog you a hundred, and if she had not made her lawful to you I shall stone you with stones. He said: And she had made her lawful to him, he said: So he was flogged a hundred. Qatadah said: So I wrote to Habib ibn Salim, and he wrote to me with this. And this hadith is not established, because Khalid ibn Urfutah is unknown; we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Qatadah, and we do not know he narrated from him except this hadith; and Shubah narrated this hadith from Abu Bishr from Habib ibn Salim from al-Numan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and Abu Bishr did not meet Habib ibn Salim."
"3238","Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar informed us, he said: Malik informed us, from Damrah ibn Said, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah. And Hawtharah ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Damrah ibn Said, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, that al-Dahhak ibn Qays asked al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him): What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite on Friday? He said: Surah al-Jumuah, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming. And we do not know these words narrated by anyone except al-Numan ibn Bashir with this chain; and it was narrated from al-Numan with wording differing from this wording."
"3239","Abdullah ibn Said al-Kindi informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris informed us, from al-Amash, from Dharr, from Yusay al-Hadrami, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3240","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr informed us, they said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Dharr, from Yusay, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Supplication is worship. And your Lord, blessed and exalted, said: Call upon Me, I shall answer you; indeed those who disdain My worship shall enter Hell abased. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3241","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh informed us, he said: Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Jabir, from Abu Azib, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Retaliation is with the sword, and for every mistake there is compensation. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from al-Numan ibn Bashir, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Numan except Abu Azib, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Azib except Jabir al-Jufi."
"3242","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali informed us, he said: Zaidah informed us, from Asim, from Khaythamah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3243","And Rizqullah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Shabbabah ibn Sawwar informed us, he said: Warqa informed us, from Asim, from Khaythamah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."
"3244","And Umar ibn Shabbah informed us of it, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Shayban informed us, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi and Khaythamah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know anyone who joined Khaythamah and al-Sha'bi together except Shayban. And this hadith was narrated from Asim by a group, and all who narrated it from Asim narrated it from Khaythamah from al-Numan except Shayban."
"3245","Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifaah informed us, he said: Nuaym ibn Abi Hind narrated to me, he said: I heard al-Sha'bi say: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of the flatterer in the affair of Allah is the likeness of a group who boarded a ship and drew lots for its places; some of them got its lowest part and some of them got its highest; then a man from those in its lowest part wanted to pierce it, so one of those in its highest part said: What are you doing? He said: I shall pierce it so I may draw water from it, and it will be easier for me than climbing up to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they leave him, he drowns and drowns them, and if they stop him, he is saved by Allah's permission and they are saved."
"3246","Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, he said: Ajlah ibn Abdullah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3247","And Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of the hadith of Nuaym ibn Abi Hind from al-Sha'bi; and we do not know Nuaym ibn Abi Hind transmitted from al-Sha'bi from al-Numan, nor from other than al-Numan, any hadith but this hadith."
"3248","Azhar ibn Jamil informed us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Shubah, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the doer of disobedience to Allah and the flatterer and the one who persists therein is the likeness of a people who drew lots in a ship; one of them had its worst and roughest and lowest part, and he only wanted to dig a hole in it; if they leave him he perishes and they perish, and if they seize his hand they are saved and he is saved."
"3249","And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us of it, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except al-Numan ibn Bashir."
"3250","Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir al-Ansari, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3251","Ali ibn Said al-Masruqi informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Al-Sari ibn Ismail informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3252","Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Said informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah informed us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays informed us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3253","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Attar informed us, he said: Al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: I read to al-Fudayl ibn Maysarah, from Abu Hariz, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Wine is from five; and Salamah ibn Kuhayl said in his hadith: Drinks are from five: wheat, barley, dates, raisins, and honey; whatever intoxicates is wine."
"3254","And Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us of it, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Israil informed us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3255","Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us, he said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3256","And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3257","And al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar informed us, he said: Malik ibn Ismail informed us, he said: Jafar ibn Ziyad al-Ahmar informed us, from Bayan and Mujalid and Abu Hayyan, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3258","Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali informed us, he said: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi informed us, from Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3259","Abu Bahr said: And Abu Awanah informed us, from al-Mughirah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3260","Ali ibn Nasr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Harun ibn Ismail al-Khazzaz informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3261","And Ahmad ibn al-Mualla al-Adami informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Muslim informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from Azrah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3262","Ali ibn al-Mundhir informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl informed us, he said: Husayn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, that his father Bashir granted him a gift, and his mother said: I shall not be content until you take the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as witness; so he came to the Prophet to take him as witness, and he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you give all your children the like of this? And in the hadith of Husayn and Mujalid he said: Did you give them the like of what you gave al-Numan? He said: No. He said: Then do not take me as witness to injustice. And in the hadith of al-Mughirah and Dawud ibn Abi Hind he said: Take another as witness; your children have a right upon you that you be just among them, as you have a right upon them that they be dutiful to you. And the hadith of Qatadah from Azrah from al-Sha'bi: we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hammam, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammam except Khalid ibn Yazid. And the hadith of Bayan: we do not know anyone who narrated it except Jafar ibn Ziyad. And the hadith of Asim al-Ahwal: we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ali ibn al-Mubarak."
"3263","Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad ibn al-Numan, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, that his father granted him a gift, and his mother Amrah bint Rawahah said: I shall not be content until you take the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as witness to that; so he came to the Prophet and he said: Did you give all your children the like of what you gave al-Numan? He said: No. He said: Then take it back."
"3264","Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Masadah informed us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir. [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3265","And Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir — by Allah, I shall not hear anyone say after him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The lawful is clear and the unlawful is clear, and between them are dubious matters; and I shall strike for you a parable of that: Allah, blessed and exalted, has made a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is what He forbade; and whoever grazes around the sanctuary is likely to fall into it, and whoever mixes is likely to cross boldly."
"3266","Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, he said: Abu Farwah informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir relate a hadith upon the minbar that I had not heard from anyone before him, nor do I think I shall hear it from anyone after him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Lawful is clear, and unlawful is clear, and doubts between them; whoever leaves them will be more leaving of what became clear to him."
"3267","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Asim, meaning Ibn Bahdalah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Lawful is clear, and unlawful is clear, and dubious matters; whoever leaves doubts clears his religion, and is likely not to fall into doubt; and whoever grazes around the sanctuary is likely to fall into it. Indeed the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions."
"3268","And al-Hasan ibn Khalaf informed us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, he said: Zakariyya, meaning Ibn Abi Zaidah, informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lawful is clear, and unlawful is clear, and dubious matters that many people do not know; whoever leaves doubts clears his religion, and is likely not to fall into doubt; and whoever grazes around the sanctuary is likely to fall into it. Indeed the sanctuary of Allah is His prohibitions."
"3269","Muhammad, nephew of Madhur, and Ahmad ibn Jamil informed us, they said: Al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer and the likeness of death is the likeness of a man with three friends: one of them is his wealth, which says: Take what you wish and leave what you wish; and another says: I am with you, I shall carry you, and when you die I shall leave you; and another says: I am with you, I enter with you and come out with you. One of them is his wealth, and another his family and child, and another his deed. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak from al-Numan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in marfu form except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl; and more than one narrated it from Simak from al-Numan in mawquf form."
"3270","Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Abu Farwah, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lawful is clear, and unlawful is clear, and dubious matters; whoever leaves doubts will be more leaving of what became clear to him."
"3271","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3272","Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us, he said: Abu Nuaym informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, he said: Al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth informed us, he said: Al-Numan ibn Bashir informed us, he said: Abu Bakr sought permission upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and heard the voice of Aishah saying: I knew that Ali is dearer to you than my father — twice or thrice. He said: So Abu Bakr sought permission and entered and lunged toward her, saying: O daughter of so-and-so, shall I not hear you raising your voice upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3273","Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us, he said: Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In man there is a morsel; when it is sound, the rest of the body is sound for it, and when it is corrupt, the rest of the body is corrupt for it: the heart."
"3274","And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us of it, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and he mentioned the like of it."
"3275","Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, he said: Yusuf ibn Khalid informed us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Amr informed us, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Al-Numan ibn Bashir addressed us, saying: O people, be merciful to one another, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with these two ears of mine say: The Muslims are like one man; when a limb of his complains, the rest of his body responds."
"3276","Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq informed us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Taymi informed us, from al-Hasan ibn Amr, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3277","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, he said: Mujalid informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3278","And al-Hasan ibn Khalaf informed us of it, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq informed us, from Zakariyya, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3279","Muhammad ibn Mamar informed us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail informed us, he said: Abu Waki informed us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah; and whoever does not thank little does not thank much; and speaking of the blessing of Allah is gratitude, and abandoning it is ingratitude; and unity is blessing, and division is punishment. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except by this route with this chain; and I did not hear anyone name the Abu Abd al-Rahman who narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi."
"3280","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: Abu Hayyan informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: My mother asked my father to grant me a gift, and he granted it to me, and she said: I shall not be content until you take the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as witness; so my father took my hand, and I was a boy, and brought me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: The mother of this one, daughter of Rawahah, pressed me for a gift to grant him, and I have granted it to him, and I take you as witness to that. He said: Have you no son besides this one? He said: Yes. He said: Did you grant him the like of what you granted this one? He said: No. He said: Then do not take me as witness, for I do not bear witness to injustice."
"3281","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Hajib ibn al-Muhallab, from his father, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir address, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Be just among your children."
"3282","Al-Fahm ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr informed us, he said: Zakariyya informed us, from Husayn ibn al-Harith Abu al-Qasim, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned his face to us and said: Straighten your rows — three times — you shall straighten your rows, or Allah shall set your faces against one another. I saw a man of us join his shoulder to his companion's shoulder, his knee to his knee, and his ankle to his ankle."
"3283","Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: Jafar ibn Awn informed us, he said: Al-Amash informed us, from Khaythamah, he said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of the believers is only like one man; when his body complains, all of it complains, and when it aches, all of it aches."
"3284","Hilal ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: My father al-Ala ibn Hilal informed us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. And we do not know Amr ibn Murrah narrated from Khaythamah from al-Numan except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Amr except al-Ala ibn Hilal alone."
"3285","Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam informed us, he said: Muammal informed us, he said: Israil informed us, he said: Abu Ishaq informed us, from a man of Bajilah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Three men set out on a journey, and the night sheltered them in a cave, and a rock fell upon the mouth of that cave. Some of them said to others: You are not on the way, and you have been afflicted with a grave matter in which nothing will avail you except to call upon the One who afflicted you with it, or words like it; so let each man of you look to the best deed he did and mention it, then call upon Allah. One of them said: O Allah, You know that I had a cousin, and there was no one on earth dearer to me than her; I sought her for herself and set for her a hundred dinars; when I sat from her as a man sits from his wife, she was seized with trembling and said: By Allah, I never committed a sin at all, and nothing drove me to it except hardship; so I stood and said: It is yours. O Allah, if You know that I only left her seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your anger, then relieve this rock from us. So the rock shifted until they saw the light. And another said: O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I had sheep I grazed nearby, and I went far and came that night delayed; I milked a vessel of milk and came to my parents and found them asleep, and I disliked waking them from their sleep; so the vessel stayed upon my hand until they woke, whenever they woke. O Allah, if You know that I only did that seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your anger, then relieve this rock from us. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So the rock broke apart until they saw the light and hoped. The third said: O Allah, if You know that I hired men for a known wage, and among them was a man who worked the work of two men; when I gave them their wages, he said: Give me the work of two men. I said: Yours is only the work of one man. He refused and left it with me and went. I kept working it for him until there gathered sixty of oxen and cows and slaves and slave-girls. He came after a while and said: O servant of Allah, is it not time you give me my wage? I said: Who are you? He said: I am the one who worked with you the work of two men, and you gave me only the work of one man, so I left it. I said: These are sixty of oxen and cows and slaves and slave-girls. He said: You detained me as you detained me, and you mock me. I said: It is yours, so take it. So he took it. O Allah, if You know that I only did that seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your anger, then relieve this rock from us. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So the rock moved away and they walked off."
"3286","And Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Adam informed us of it, he said: Muammal informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. Except that he said the first one said: I had a cousin among the most beautiful of women, and she was the dearest of people to me; I proposed to her father, and he refused to marry her to me, so I went off; and her father died and I returned and she was in need; she sent to me complaining of need, and I said: Nothing except that you give me yourself. She did that repeatedly, then her need grew severe, and she sent to me the third or fourth time, and she gave me hope of herself, so I came to her; when I sat from her as a man sits from his wife, she was seized with trembling and said: I adjure you by Allah not to break this seal except by its right, for by Allah I never did this deed at all. So I stood from her and returned her self to her, and gave her her bridal gift. O Allah, if You know that I did that only seeking Your pleasure and fearing Your anger, then relieve us. And we do not know anyone who transmitted it in musnad form from Hammad ibn Salamah from Simak from al-Numan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Muammal; and Abu Sad Said ibn al-Marzuban narrated it from Simak from al-Numan ibn Bashir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3287","Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili informed us of it, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan Abu Masud al-Zajjaj informed us, he said: Abu Sad informed us, from Simak, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Sad except Abu Masud, and he was trustworthy; and we do not know Abu Sad transmitted in musnad form from Simak except this hadith, nor did we hear it except from Ali ibn Harb; and Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated it from al-Numan ibn Bashir."
"3288","Salamah ibn Shabib informed us, he said: Ismail ibn Abd al-Karim informed us, from Abd al-Samad ibn Maqil, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And the hadith of Abu Ishaq from a man of Bajilah: we do not know anyone who named him except Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah from his father from al-Amash from Abu Ishaq, who said: from Amr ibn Shurahbil from al-Numan ibn Bashir; and Amr ibn Shurahbil is Bajali."
"3289","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Kufi Abu Shaybah informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah informed us, from his father, from al-Amash. And Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Rayhan ibn Said informed us, from Abbad, meaning Ibn Mansur, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wants to pray at night, let him take a handful of dust and place it beside him; when he wakes, let him throw it to his right and to his left. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route with this chain."
"3290","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sun and moon eclipse, pray as the most recent prayer you prayed. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Hisham, nor from Hisham except Muadh, his son."
"3291","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Numan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3292","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from al-Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jarmi, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, wrote a book before He created the earth by two thousand years; He sent down in it two verses with which He sealed Surah al-Baqarah; they are not recited in a house three nights and a devil approaches it. [The Arabic syntax makes the devil keeping away the intended meaning: no devil comes near it.]"
"3293","Khalid ibn Yusuf informed us of it, he said: My father informed us, he said: Abu Raja Muhammad ibn Sayf informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Salih al-Ashari, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani transmitted in musnad form from al-Numan ibn Bashir except this hadith, and we do not know Abu Raja transmitted from Abu Qilabah except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from him except Yusuf ibn Khalid."
"3294","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, he said: Al-Amash informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the one who upholds the bounds of Allah and the flatterer therein is the likeness of a people who drew lots upon a ship at sea; some of them got its highest part and some its lowest; and those in its lowest would come out and draw water and burden those in its highest. Those in its highest said: We shall not let you pass over us and harm us. Those in its lowest said: If you stop us, we shall open a door from its lowest. If they seize their hands and stop them, all are saved; and if they leave them, all perish."
"3295","Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith informed us, he said: Jafar ibn Awn informed us, he said: Al-Amash informed us, he said: I heard Amir say: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The likeness of the believers is only like one man; when he complains, the rest of the body responds with sleeplessness and fever."
"3296","Musnad of Qurrah ibn Iyas al-Muzani (may Allah be pleased with him). Musnad of Qurrah ibn Iyas al-Muzani from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3297","And Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting three days of every month is fasting the whole year and breaking it. And we do not know any route for this hadith from Qurrah ibn Iyas except this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qurrah ibn Iyas except his son Muawiyah ibn Qurrah."
"3298","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Shubah, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a son of his, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you love him? He said: May Allah love you as I love him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and asked about him, and they said: His son died. So he came to him and said: Would it not please you not to come to any gate of Paradise but find him there opening it for you. And we do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Qurrah ibn Iyas."
"3299","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Syria perish, there is no good in you; and people of my nation shall ever remain upon the truth, dominant over people, until the Day of Resurrection. And we do not know this hadith with this wording narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Qurrah ibn Iyas."
"3300","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali informed us, they said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having milked and tied the udder; and he only meant that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as an active boy."
"3301","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali informed us, they said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab informed us, he said: Shubah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, that Abdullah ibn Masud climbed a tree to pick a tooth-stick from it, and placed his legs upon it, and the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at the thinness of his legs. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are heavier in the Scale than Uhud. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shubah except Sahl ibn Hammad."
"3302","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi informed us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai informed us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father. [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3303","And Zurayq ibn al-Sakht informed us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Our food in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was only the two blacks, meaning dates and water. And Rawh ibn Ubadah said: Dates and water. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah except Bistam ibn Muslim, and he is a well-known man of Basra; Shubah and others narrated from him."
"3304","Abdullah ibn Muawiyah al-Jumahi informed us, he said: Furat ibn Abi al-Furat informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with his buttons undone."
"3305","And Amr ibn Ali and Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Tai informed us of it, they said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muawiyah, informed us, from Urwah ibn Abdullah ibn Qushayr, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And he added in it: So I never saw Muawiyah except with his buttons undone."
"3306","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Amir informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Maysarah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of these two trees, let him not approach our mosque; and if you must do it, kill them by cooking. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah except Khalid ibn Maysarah, and more than one narrated from him."
"3307","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Awwam informed us, he said: Said ibn Sallam informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Maysarah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sat, his Companions would sit with him in circles. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Khalid ibn Maysarah except Said ibn Sallam; and Said is weak in hadith, and only what is unique to him is written, with the defect explained in that."
"3308","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Harun Abu Muslim informed us, from Qatadah, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We were forbidden from prayer between the pillars and were driven from it with driving in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3309","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad informed us, he said: Harun Abu Muslim informed us, from Qatadah, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, with the like of it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Harun, and we do not know Qatadah traced in musnad form from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from his father except this hadith."
"3310","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid informed us, he said: Qurrah, meaning Ibn Khalid, informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sought his permission to see the Seal; so I put my hand into his pocket and found upon the cartilage of his shoulder something like a lump. And we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from his father except Qurrah ibn Khalid."
"3311","Abdullah ibn al-Waddah al-Kufi informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi Karimah, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a man who had consummated marriage with his father's wife, or married his father's wife, and ordered that his neck be struck. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from his father except Khalid ibn Abi Karimah, nor from Khalid except Ibn Idris; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Idris except Yusuf ibn Manazil and Abdullah ibn al-Waddah; and others narrate it from Ibn Idris from Khalid ibn Abi Karimah from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah in mursal form."
"3312","Amr ibn Malik informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti informed us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, meaning al-Jassas, informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. And we do not know anyone who narrated it except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan from Ziyad; and Ziyad is a man of Basra, sound in hadith."
"3313","And Abu al-Sabbah Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Ali ibn Mushir informed us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: I love them both, so love them both — or he said: O Allah, I love them both, so love them both. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ziyad except Ali ibn Mushir, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ali except Khalid ibn Makhlad; and we heard it only from Muhammad ibn al-Layth from Khalid."
"3314","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad informed us — the wording is Abd al-Quddus's — they said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam informed us, he said: Al-Azhar ibn Sinan informed us, from Shabib ibn Muhammad ibn Wasi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I was with my father heading for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when we were partway, we passed a tribe and spent the night there, and the shepherd came to the people of the tribe running, saying: I shall not graze for you, for the wolf comes every night and takes a sheep from the flock, while the idol watches, neither changing nor objecting. They said: Stay with us — I think he said: until we come to him — so they came to him and spoke around him, and he said to the shepherd: Stay tonight. My father said: I shall stay tonight to see. So we spent our night; when it was the dawn prayer, the shepherd came rushing to the people of the village, saying to them: Glad tidings — do you not see that the wolf is tied before the idol with no rope. So they came, and we came with them. He said: So he said: Yes, do so. Then we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and my father related the story to him, and he said: Satan toys with them. And we do not know this hadith narrated with this wording except from Qurrah ibn Iyas, and we do not know any route for it besides this route; and al-Azhar ibn Sinan was narrated from by Yazid ibn Harun and Muhammad ibn Jahdam and others."
"3315","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi and Muammal ibn Hisham informed us, they said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim, and he is Ibn Ulayyah, informed us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when I slaughter a sheep I feel mercy for it. He said: And the sheep — if you show it mercy, Allah shows you mercy."
"3316","Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Susi informed us — the wording is Ahmad ibn Yahya's — they said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar informed us, he said: My father al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham narrated to me, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Mahdi, saying: He shall fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with wrong and injustice."
"3317","Uqbah ibn Mukram informed us, he said: Muadh ibn Asad informed us, he said: Kathir ibn Abdullah informed us, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Uqbah ibn Mukram from Muadh ibn Asad; we heard it only from him."
"3318","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Jad informed us, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, when I slaughter a sheep I feel mercy for it. He said: And the sheep — if you show it mercy, Allah shows you mercy."
"3319","Ismail ibn Abi al-Harith and Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Susi informed us, they said: Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham informed us, he said: Al-Muhabbar ibn Qahdham informed us, from his father Qahdham ibn Sulayman, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth shall be filled with wrong and injustice; when it is filled with wrong and injustice, Allah sends a man from me whose name is my name, or whose name is my father's name; he fills it with justice and equity as it was filled with wrong and injustice. Neither the heaven withholds anything of its rain, nor the earth anything of its produce. He remains among you seven, or eight, or nine — meaning years. And this hadith was narrated by Mamar from Abu Harun al-Abdi from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah from Abu al-Siddiq from Abu Said from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and it is more likely from Abu Said, because it was narrated from Abu Said by various routes; and we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this chain."
"3320","Musnad of Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him). Musnad of Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and it is said: his name is Alqamah. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, they said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys."
"3321","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Shaybani informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was fasting on a journey; when the sun set, he said to a man: Dismount and mix sawiq for us. He said: O Messenger of Allah, if only it were evening. He said: Dismount and mix sawiq for us. He said: O Messenger of Allah, daylight is still upon you. He said: Dismount and mix sawiq for us. So he dismounted and mixed, and the Messenger of Allah drank, then said: When you see the night approaching from here, the fasting one has broken fast. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, and we do not know any route for it from him except al-Shaybani."
"3322","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, they said: Abu Muawiyah informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade nabidh of the jar. I said: Which jar? He said: I do not know. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa except from the hadith of al-Shaybani; and more than one narrated it from al-Shaybani, so we sufficed with those we mentioned. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Taymi from al-Shaybani except Hammad ibn Masadah."
"3323","Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Zuhri informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Masadah informed us, from al-Taymi, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3324","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Sulayman al-Shaybani informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned."
"3325","Al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, as I think, he said: Hushaym informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jew and a Jewess. And the hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he stoned a Jew and a Jewess: we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Shaybani except Hushaym alone."
"3326","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Yafur, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seven campaigns, eating locusts."
"3327","Al-Hasan ibn Mudrik informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad informed us, he said: Abu Awanah informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We fought with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seven campaigns, eating locusts. And the hadith of al-Shaybani: we did not hear anyone narrate it except al-Hasan ibn Mudrik from Yahya ibn Hammad, and with him is the hadith of Abu Yafur. And this hadith from al-Shaybani: we did not hear anyone narrate it from Abu Awanah from al-Shaybani except al-Hasan from Yahya ibn Hammad from Abu Awanah. And what is with Abu Awanah is from Abu Yafur from Ibn Abi Awfa: more than one informed us from Abu Awanah from Abu Yafur. And al-Hasan ibn Mudrik mentioned this hadith from Yahya ibn Hammad from Abu Awanah from al-Shaybani and from Abu Yafur from Ibn Abi Awfa."
"3328","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise of hollow pearl, with no noise in it and no toil."
"3329","Azhar ibn Jamil informed us, he said: Al-Nadr ibn Ismail informed us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Khadijah glad tidings of a house of hollow pearl. Ismail said: So it was said to Ibn Abi Awfa: Hollow pearl? He said: Pearl hollow. And this hadith was narrated by Ismail ibn Abi Khalid and al-Shaybani and Salamah ibn Kuhayl, all from Ibn Abi Awfa. As for the hadith of al-Shaybani, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated it from him, and none followed Abu Bakr in it."
"3330","And as for the hadith of Salamah ibn Kuhayl, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Yahya ibn Salamah informed us of it, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not present in the source text of this row.]"
"3331","Muhammad ibn Muammal informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal informed us, he said: Imran informed us, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa. [The matn of the prophetic report is not present in this row; the row is an isnad note as in the source.]"
"3332","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, he said: Amr ibn Asim informed us, he said: Imran informed us, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is with the judge so long as he does not wrong — or he said: The hand of Allah is with the judge so long as he does not wrong."
"3333","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal informed us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from al-Husayn ibn Abdullah, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Shaybani except Imran; so Muhammad ibn Bilal inserted between Ammar and al-Shaybani Husayn ibn Abdullah, and we do not know who this Husayn ibn Abdullah is."
"3334","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, informed us, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate against the Confederates, saying: O Allah, Sender of the Book, swift in reckoning, defeat the Confederates and shake them. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except from the hadith of Ismail from Ibn Abi Awfa; and more than one narrated it from Ismail."
"3335","Bishr ibn Khalid informed us, he said: Abu Usamah informed us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed umrah and circumambulated the House, then went out to circuit between al-Safa and al-Marwah; and we shielded him so none of the people of Makkah would strike him, or one of them would throw something at him. And we do not know any route for this hadith from Ibn Abi Awfa except this route; and more than one narrated it from Ismail."
"3336","3340 - Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami and Hilal ibn al-'Ala' informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: 'Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No one who witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah will enter the Hellfire. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except 'Isa ibn Yunus, nor from 'Isa except 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far."
"3337","3341 - Tamim ibn al-Muntasir al-Wasiti informed us, saying: Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, from Sharik, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House and shaved in his 'umrah. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Isma'il with this wording from Ibn Abi Awfa except Sharik."
"3338","3342 - Al-Sari ibn Yahya, nephew of Hannad, informed us, saying: Qabisah ibn 'Uqbah informed us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Salih informed us, from Abu al-Ya'fur, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: I witnessed him and he pronounced four takbirs over a funeral, then stood for a while meaning he supplicated, then said: You thought I was going to pronounce five takbirs? They said: No. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pronounce four takbirs."
"3339","3343 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far, meaning Ibn Abi Muwatiyah, informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed us, from 'Ammar ibn Sayf, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to his Companions when they were all gathered, and said: This night I was shown your dwellings in Paradise and how near your dwellings are. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Abu Bakr and said: O Abu Bakr, I know a man - I know his name and the name of his father and his mother - there is no gate of Paradise he comes to but it will be said to him: Welcome, welcome. Salman said to him: This one is of lofty rank, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He is Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah. Then he turned to 'Umar and said: O 'Umar, I saw in Paradise a palace of white pearl, its balconies of white pearls, inlaid with ruby. I said: Whose is this? It was said: For a young man of Quraysh. I thought it was mine, so I went to enter it, but he said: O Muhammad, this belongs to 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. Nothing kept me from entering it except your jealousy, O Abu Hafs. 'Umar wept and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you - would I be jealous with regard to you, O Messenger of Allah? Then he turned to 'Uthman ibn 'Affan and said: O 'Uthman, every Prophet has a companion in Paradise, and you are my companion in Paradise. Then he took the hand of 'Ali and said: O 'Ali, would you not be pleased that your dwelling in Paradise be facing my dwelling? He said: Yes, indeed, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Your dwelling in Paradise will be facing my dwelling. Then he turned to Talhah and al-Zubayr and said: O Talhah and O Zubayr, every Prophet has a disciple, and you two are my disciples. Then he turned to 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf and said: You were held back from me among my Companions until I feared you had perished and drowned in a severe drowning. I said: What held you back? He said: O Messenger of Allah, because of my abundant wealth I remained detained, called to account; I was asked about my wealth - from where I earned it and on what I spent it. 'Abd al-Rahman wept and said: O Messenger of Allah, these are one hundred riding camels that came to me tonight from the merchants of Egypt, and I call you to witness that they are for the people of Madinah and their children, so that Allah may lighten that Day for me. 'Ammar ibn Sayf is righteous, 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muharibi is trustworthy, Ibn Abi Muwatiyah is righteous, and the rest of the chain is not questioned because of their trustworthiness. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa except through this channel with this chain."
"3340","3344 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd and Taliq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti informed us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman informed us, saying: Yazid ibn 'Ata' informed us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only combined Hajj and 'Umrah because he knew he would not perform Hajj after that year of his. This hadith - Yazid ibn 'Ata' erred in it when he narrated it from Isma'il from Ibn Abi Awfa; rather what is correct is from Isma'il from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated it from Isma'il from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3341","3345 - Nasr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Abu Ahmad informed us, saying: Mis'ar informed us, from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Ibn Abi Awfa. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3342","3346 - Nasr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Abu Ahmad informed us, saying: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Ibn Abi Awfa. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3343","3347 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and al-Hasan ibn 'Uthman informed us of it, saying: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd informed us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, saying: Yazid Abu Khalid narrated to me, from Ibrahim, meaning al-Saksaki, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him of forgetting the Qur'an, saying: Teach me something that will suffice me. He said: Say: In the name of Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah. He said: He counted them on his hand, then closed his five fingers and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for my Lord, so what is for me? He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, grant me well-being, provide for me, and guide me. He said: He counted them on his hand, five, and closed his other fingers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for this one, he has filled his hands with good. This hadith - we do not know it narrated except from Ibn Abi Awfa from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibrahim al-Saksaki is Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, and Yazid Abu Khalid is Yazid al-Dalani."
"3344","3348 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-'Askari informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Ibrahim, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man displayed his goods after 'Asr and swore falsely by Allah that he had been offered such-and-such for them, so this verse was revealed: Indeed those who purchase with the covenant of Allah and their oaths a small price. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except through this channel."
"3345","3349 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Kufi al-Sayrafi informed us, saying: Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed us, saying: al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The najish (one who falsely bids up a price) consumes riba. This hadith - more than one narrator narrated it from Ibn Abi Awfa as mawquf, and we do not know anyone who narrated it marfu' from Hafs except Ibrahim ibn Yusuf."
"3346","3350 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Aban informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from Mis'ar, from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Ibn Abi Awfa. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3347","3351 - 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala' wrote to me informing that Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to him from Mis'ar, from Ibrahim al-Saksaki, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah, blessed and exalted, are those who watch the sun and the moon. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mis'ar with this chain except Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah. Muhammad ibn al-Walid, who narrated this hadith to us - we do not know anyone who corroborated him in his narration from Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr from Ibn 'Uyaynah. The hadith is only known as that of 'Abd al-Jabbar. What is correct is what was narrated from Mis'ar from Ibrahim from a man from Abu al-Darda' as mawquf."
"3348","3352 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Samad informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, saying: Abu al-Mukhtar informed us, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who serves drink to the people is the last of them. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except through this channel with this chain."
"3349","3353 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When charity was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he would say: O Allah, bless the family of so-and-so. Then my father brought him his charity, and he said: O Allah, bless the family of Abu Awfa. This hadith - we do not know of a path for it from Ibn Abi Awfa except this path. And we do not know that 'Amr ibn Murrah heard from any of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Ibn Abi Awfa."
"3350","3354 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Firas, from Mudrik ibn 'Umarah, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does he steal when he steals while he is a believer, nor does he plunder a plunder of value - or he said: of honor - which he seizes while he is a believer. This hadith - we do not know of a path for it from Ibn Abi Awfa except this path."
"3351","3355 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A daughter of his died, and he followed her on a mule walking behind the funeral, while women were lamenting her. Ibn Abi Awfa said: Do not lament, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade lamentations; rather let each of you shed from her tears whatever she wills. Then he prayed over her and pronounced four takbirs, then stood after the fourth for the duration between two takbirs, seeking forgiveness for her and supplicating. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do thus. He said: And the crier of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out to overturn the pots, so we overturned them. We do not know that Ibrahim al-Hajari narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except this hadith."
"3352","3356 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn al-Walid informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Mijza'ah ibn Zahir, from Ibn Abi Awfa. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3353","3357 - Abu Kurayb informed us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Yazid ibn Mardanabah informed us, saying: Raqabah, meaning Ibn Masqalah, informed us, from Mijza'ah ibn Zahir, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: O Allah, purify me with snow and hail and cold water; O Allah, purify me of sins and cleanse me of them as the white garment is cleansed of filth."
"3354","3358 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd informed us, saying: Sa'd ibn 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad informed us, from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, that 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on one of his days in which he met the enemy, stood among the people and addressed them, saying: Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being; but if you meet them then be patient, and know that Paradise is beneath the shadows of swords. Then he supplicated, saying: O Allah, Revealer of the Book, Defeater of the Confederates, defeat them and grant us victory over them. This hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Ibn Abi Awfa."
"3355","3359 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah informed us, saying: Hafs ibn 'Umar informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, to You belongs praise filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter."
"3356","3360 - Ahmad ibn Dawud informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Abu Malik al-Nakha'i informed us, from Sufyan ibn Abi Habibah, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When his wife died he would say: Carry her and show eagerness to carry her, for she used to carry with her freed slaves by night the stones of the mosque which was founded upon piety, while we by day would carry two stones at a time."
"3357","3361 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, saying: al-A'mash informed us, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from Ibn Abi Awfa. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3358","3362 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Abu Dawud informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Hasan, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, to You belongs praise filling the heavens and the earth and filling whatever You will of anything thereafter."
"3359","3363 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Kufi informed us, saying: 'Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath informed us, from his father, from al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah, from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, purify me with snow and hail and cold water; O Allah, cleanse me of sins and faults as the white garment is cleansed of filth. We do not know that 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except this hadith, and none narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn 'Ubaydullah from 'Ata' except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"3360","3364 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-'Askari narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, saying: I saw on the shin of 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa a wound, and I said: What is this? He said: I was struck with it alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn."
"3361","3365 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn 'Awn informed us, saying: Abu Isma'il Ibrahim ibn Sulayman informed us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf complained of Khalid ibn al-Walid to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Why do you harm a man from among the Companions of Badr? Even if you spent the like of Uhud in gold you would not reach his deed. He said: They revile me and I do not answer them. He said: Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah, which Allah unsheathed against the disbelievers."
"3362","3366 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Sulayman informed us, saying: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya informed us, from Muhammad ibn 'Awn al-Khurasani, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The destructive things are three: a man's admiration of himself, greed that is obeyed, and desire that is followed."
"3363","3367 - Isma'il said: And Muhammad ibn 'Awn narrated to me, from Yahya ibn 'Uqayl, from Ibn Abi Awfa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3364","3368 - Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas informed us, saying: Salamah ibn Raja' informed us, saying: al-Sha'tha', a woman of Banu al-Asad, narrated to me, saying: I entered upon Ibn Abi Awfa and saw him pray Fajr as two rak'ahs. His wife said: You only prayed two rak'ahs. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two rak'ahs when he was given glad tidings of the conquest, and when he was given glad tidings of the head of Abu Jahl. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Ibn Abi Awfa, and we do not know for it a path except this path."
"3365","3369 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us, saying: Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibn Abi Awfa. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3366","3370 - Al-Walid ibn 'Amr informed us of it, saying: Ya'qub informed us, saying: Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I asked him: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leave a will? He said: No. I said: How was the will prescribed upon the people and they were commanded with it, yet he did not leave a will? He said: He left as a will the Book of Allah. Huzayl ibn Shurahbil said: Abu Bakr used to take charge over the legatee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu Bakr wished he had found in that a covenant from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he pierced his nose with its nose-ring."
"3367","3371 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: al-Hajjaj ibn Farrukh informed us, from al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When Bilal said: The prayer has commenced, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would rise with the takbir. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa with this chain."
"3368","3372 - Ahmad ibn Thabit informed us, saying: 'Umar ibn 'Imran informed us, saying: Abu Sa'd informed us, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I prayed with him over a funeral, and he pronounced four takbirs over it, then paused a little until we intended that he would pronounce a fifth. Then he said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. Then he heard women weeping and said: We were forbidden from eulogizing. And he said to his servant: Where am I? He said: In front of the funeral. He said: Put me behind the funeral."
"3369","3373 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya informed us, saying: Shadh ibn al-Fayyad informed us, saying: Hashim ibn Sa'id informed us, from Zubayd, from Ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with three rak'ahs, reciting in them: in the first, Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; in the second, Say: O disbelievers; and in the third, Say: He is Allah, the One. When he gave salam he would say: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy, prolonging his voice with it. This hadith - Hashim ibn Sa'id erred in it, because the trustworthy narrators narrate it from Zubayd from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza from his father from Ubayy from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Hashim added in his hadith: When he gave salam he said: Glory be to the Sovereign, the Most Holy - and this is not in the hadith of anyone else."
"3370","3374 - Salamah ibn Shabib informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi informed us, saying: Fayid Abu al-Warqa' informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa al-Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a need of Allah, blessed and exalted, or of anyone, let him say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. I ask You for what necessitates Your mercy and the resolves of Your forgiveness, and the spoils of every righteousness, and safety from every sin and every offense. Leave no sin of mine unforgiven, no worry undispelled, and no need with which You are pleased unfulfilled, O Most Merciful of the merciful. This hadith - we only mentioned it from Fayid, though Fayid is not strong, because we did not retain the wording of this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this chain, so for that reason we mentioned it."
"3371","3375 - Salamah informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi informed us, saying: Fayid informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a boy came to him and said: May my father be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah - an orphan boy with an orphan sister and a widowed mother. Feed us; may Allah give you from what is with Him until you are pleased. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How excellent is what you have said, O boy. Go to our household and bring us whatever food you find with them. Bilal then came with twenty-one dates and placed them in the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured with his palms toward his mouth, with the dates in them, while we thought he was supplicating for blessing upon the dates. Then he said: O boy, seven for you, seven for your mother, and seven for your sister; eat dinner with one date and lunch with another. When the boy left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Mu'adh ibn Jabal stood up to him, placed his hand on his head, and said: May Allah mend your orphanhood and make you a successor of your father. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have seen what I did with the boy, O Mu'adh? He said: O Messenger of Allah, out of mercy for the boy. At that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no Muslim takes charge of an orphan and discharges his charge well but Allah will grant him a degree for every hair, give him a good deed for every hair, and expiate from him an evil deed for every hair. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from any channel except this channel from Ibn Abi Awfa. We have already mentioned our note on Fayid."
"3372","3376 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Abi Yahya al-Kufi informed us, saying: Khazim ibn Husayn Abu Ishaq al-Humaysi informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Juhadah informed us, from Tarafah al-Hadrami, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to lead us in Zuhr when the sun declined, even if a grain were placed on the scorching ground it would cook it. Then he would prolong the first rak'ah, remaining standing reciting as long as he heard the clatter of the people's sandals, then bow. Then he would stand in the second and bow a rak'ah shorter than the first rak'ah, then make the third rak'ah shorter than the second and the fourth shorter than the third. Then he would pray 'Asr while the sun was white and clear, for the duration a traveler walks two or three farsakhs. He would prolong the first rak'ah of 'Asr and make the second shorter than the first. He would pray Maghrib when one would say: Has the sun set or not? He would prolong the first rak'ah of Maghrib, make the second shorter than the first and the third shorter than the second. And he would delay the last 'Isha' prayer somewhat. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except through this channel with this chain."
"3373","3377 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah informed us, saying: Bishr ibn Muhammad ibn Aban informed us, saying: Ziyad ibn Abi Muslim Abu 'Umar al-Saffar informed us, saying: I heard Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani say: Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah sent me to 'Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa. I arrived with some Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with me, and I said: What do you command the people with? He said: Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me: if I live to see anything of these turmoils, to take my sword and break it and sit in my house. If I am entered upon in my house, he said: Sit in your inner chamber; if you are entered upon there, kneel on your knees and say: I bear your sin and my sin, so you will be among the companions of the Fire, and that is the recompense of the wrongdoers. So I have broken my sword; when I am entered upon in my house I enter my inner chamber, and when I am entered upon in my inner chamber I kneel on my knees and say what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to say. We do not know that Abu al-Ash'ath narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except this hadith. Ziyad ibn Abi Muslim is a well-known man of Basrah."
"3374","3378 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari informed us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, saying: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Asma' bint Zayd ibn al-Khattab, from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command ablution for every prayer, then he left that and commanded them with the siwak for every prayer. These words - we do not know anyone who narrated them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib, who is said to be the son of Ghasil al-Mala'ikah (the one washed by the angels). We do not know for it a path except this path. Hanzalah ibn al-Rahib is the one whom the angels washed, because he was martyred on the day of Uhud while in a state of janabah."
"3375","3379 - 'Abd al-Samad ibn Sulayman al-Muqri' informed us, saying: al-'Ala' ibn Sinan informed us, saying: 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar informed us, from Damdam ibn Jaws, from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulating the House upon his mount, touching the Corner with his mihjan (hooked staff). This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar except al-'Ala' ibn Sinan."
"3376","3380 - Harun ibn Sufyan informed us, saying: 'Asim ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah informed us, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from 'Abdullah ibn Yazid, from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah, who said: We were in the house of Qays ibn Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah, with some Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with us. We said to him: Come forward. He said: I would not do that. 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has most right to the front of his bedding, most right to the front of his mount, and most right to lead prayer in his house. So he commanded a freed slave of his, who came forward and prayed. This hadith - we do not know for it a path from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah except this path."
"3377","3381 - Abu al-Saqr al-Warraq informed us, saying: Husayn ibn Muhammad informed us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dirham of riba which a man consumes knowingly is worse than thirty-six acts of adultery. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah from him. Some narrated it from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from a man from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah."
"3378","3382 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, saying: my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, who said: I said to him: Do you see the ablution of 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar for every prayer - from whom did he take it? He said: Asma' bint Zayd ibn al-Khattab narrated to him from 'Abdullah ibn Hanzalah that he narrated to her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command ablution at every prayer, and when that became burdensome for them he commanded the siwak at every prayer."
"3379","3383 - 'Ali ibn Sahl al-Mada'ini informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to command Zakat al-Fitr on the day of Fitr before praying the 'Id prayer, and would recite this verse: He has succeeded who purifies himself, and remembers the name of his Lord and prays. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Amr ibn 'Awf. We do not know anyone who narrated it from 'Amr ibn 'Awf except his son 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, nor anyone who narrated it from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr except Kathir ibn 'Abdullah."
"3380","3384 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I fear for my ummah three things: the slip of a scholar, followed desire, and an unjust judgment."
"3381","3385 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf al-Muzani informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives a sunnah of mine that has died out after me will have the like of the reward of those among the people who act upon it, without anything diminishing from their rewards. And whoever innovates a bid'ah with which Allah and His Messenger are not pleased will bear the like of the burdens of those among the people who act upon it, without anything being lessened from their burdens."
"3382","3386 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad informed us, saying: Abu Uways informed us, from Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"3383","3387 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day urged charity. 'Ulbah ibn Zayd stood and said: I have nothing but my honor; I call you to witness, O Messenger of Allah, that I have given my honor in charity to whoever wronged me. Then he sat. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is 'Ulbah ibn Zayd? - saying it two or three times. 'Ulbah stood and he said: You are the one who gave your honor in charity; Allah has accepted it from you."
"3384","3388 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hour that is hoped for on Friday is from when the imam comes out until he finishes the sermon."
"3385","3389 - Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronounced seven takbirs in the two 'Ids - seven in the first and five in the last."
"3386","3390 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world will not end until there is a garrison of Muslims at a place called Bulan, until they fight the Banu al-Asfar, striving in the path of Allah, not caring in Allah for the blame of any blamer, until Allah grants them victory over Constantinople and Rome through tasbih and takbir - its fortress will be demolished - and until they divide wealth with shields. He said: Then a crier will cry out: O people of Islam, the False Messiah, the Dajjal, has come out among your lands and homes. They will say: Who is this crier? They will not know who he is, so they will send a scout to see whether he is the Messiah. They will return to them saying: We saw nothing and heard nothing. They will say: By Allah, the crier only cried out from the heaven or from the earth. Come, let us all go out; if the Messiah is there we will fight him until Allah judges between us and him, and He is the best of judges. And if it is the other matter, then these are your lands and your troops and your kinsfolk - you will have returned to them."
"3387","3391 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf al-Muzani informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever brandishes weapons against us is not of us."
"3388","3392 - Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zakat upon the Muslims is a sa' of dates, or a sa' of raisins, or a sa' of barley, or a sa' of dried yogurt."
"3389","3393 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives dead land that is not in the rightful possession of a Muslim, it belongs to him; and the unjust root has no right. And the Muslims abide by their conditions."
"3390","3394 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn 'Athmah informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things of the affairs of Jahiliyyah the people will not abandon, or will not leave: impugning lineage, wailing, and their saying: We were given rain by such-and-such lunar mansion or by such-and-such star."
"3391","3395 - al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah informed us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, meaning al-Hunayni, informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted Bilal ibn al-Harith al-Muzani the mines of the Qabaliyyah region, both its highlands and lowlands, and where cultivation is viable of Quds."
"3392","3396 - With its chain: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command the use of ithmid (antimony) at bedtime."
"3393","3397 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam began as something strange and will return as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers."
"3394","3398 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Khalid informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr informed us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not intercept incoming caravans, and let no townsman sell for a Bedouin."
"3395","3399 - 'Abdullah ibn Shabib informed us, saying: Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah informed us, saying: Kathir ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he arrived in Madinah, and he prayed toward Bayt al-Maqdis for seventeen months, then he turned toward the Ka'bah. Abu Bakr said: And this 'Amr ibn 'Awf - we have explained that none narrated from him except his son. Only such of his hadiths are written as none other narrates. Kathir's hadith - others shared in narrating it, so we mentioned among his hadiths ones none other narrated, and ones others narrated, so that it be known that some of his hadith was shared in narration from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The end of the twenty-eighth juz', and praise be to Allah abundantly as He deserves, and the beginning of the twenty-ninth."
"3396","3400 - Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd al-Khaliq informed us, saying: Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, saying: Waki' informed us, saying: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We discussed ghusl from janabah in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: As for me, I pour three handfuls upon my head."
"3397","3401 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Surad, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. This hadith has a sound chain. The like of these words was narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels. The highest who narrated that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording is Jubayr ibn Mut'im. We do not know for Jubayr ibn Mut'im a chain other than this chain. A group narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, so we sufficed with the hadith of al-Thawri and Shu'bah to the exclusion of others. Sulayman ibn Surad has companionship; he narrated more than one hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We do not know anyone among the Companions who narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except Sulayman ibn Surad and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar."
"3398","3402 - Muhammad ibn Sudran informed us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Talhah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Awf, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Qurashi has the strength of two men of other than Quraysh. It was said: What did he mean by that? He said: In soundness of judgment."
"3399","3403 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided the share of the near kindred between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, I came to him, I and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, these Banu Hashim - we do not deny their merit because of your station which Allah granted you among them. So why is it that you gave Banu al-Muttalib and withheld from us, though we and they are to you in one station? He said: They did not separate from me in Jahiliyyah nor in Islam; Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one thing - and he interlaced his fingers. This hadith - more than one narrated it from al-Zuhri from Sa'id from Jubayr, and that is correct. It was narrated from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr from his father; the hadith of Sa'id is more correct. We do not retain these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with the narration of Jubayr ibn Mut'im from him."
"3400","3404 - Nasr ibn 'Ali and Ahmad ibn 'Abdah informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had Mut'im ibn 'Adiyy been alive and then interceded with me for these foul-smelling ones, I would have granted his intercession for them. This hadith has a sound chain. We do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a connected channel with a sound chain other than this channel."
"3401","3405 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The severer of kinship ties will not enter Paradise. This hadith with this wording - we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Jubayr ibn Mut'im. The like of these words was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with other than this wording. The chain of this hadith is sound."
"3402","3406 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah and Nasr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3403","3407 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: Malik informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3404","3408 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, saying: I heard Burd, meaning Ibn Sinan, narrating from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3405","3409 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali and 'Abdah ibn 'Abdullah informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. The wording is the wording of Sufyan, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting al-Tur in Maghrib. Muhammad ibn 'Amr added in his hadith from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the ransom of the people of Badr, and I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in Maghrib while leading the people: By the Tur, and a Book inscribed. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Jubayr ibn Mut'im. We do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from any channel that he recited al-Tur in Maghrib except in this hadith."
"3406","3410 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah informed us, saying: Sufyan, meaning Ibn 'Uyaynah, informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3407","3411 - 'Umar ibn Musa al-Sami informed us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3408","3412 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn Husayn informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3409","3413 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: 'Affan informed us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, who is Abu Bishr, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have names: I am Muhammad and Ahmad and al-'Aqib and al-Mahi and al-Hashir, before whom the people will be gathered; and al-'Aqib is the last of the Prophets. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Jubayr ibn Mut'im with this chain. We do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah other than Hammad ibn Salamah. We do not know that Ja'far ibn Abi Wahshiyyah narrated from Nafi' ibn Jubayr other than this hadith. Its chain is sound."
"3410","3414 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Numayr informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq - and to the best of my knowledge he said: from 'Abd al-Salam - from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3411","3415 - Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi informed us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3412","3416 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: And 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to me, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: May Allah brighten a man who hears my saying, retains it, and conveys it as he heard it; for often a bearer of fiqh conveys to one more understanding than him, and often a bearer of fiqh is not a faqih."
"3413","3417 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, saying: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. He added in it: Three things over which the heart of a believing man harbors no malice: sincerity of deed for Allah, good counsel to the rulers, and adherence to the congregation; for their supplication encompasses them. This hadith - the like of its words was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels. The wording of Jubayr's hadith differs from the wording of those hadiths, though close to their wordings. This 'Abd al-Salam I deem to be 'Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Janub, though he did not attribute him; he is weak in hadith. Abu Damrah and Abu Ma'shar narrated from him. The hadith of Abu al-Huwayrith from Muhammad ibn Jubayr - we do not know anyone who narrated it marfu' except Ibn Ishaq from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr. None narrated it from Ibn Ishaq except Ibrahim ibn Sa'd. Al-Darawardi narrated it from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, saying: from Abu al-Huwayrith from Muhammad ibn Jubayr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), without saying: from his father. Muhammad ibn Ishaq is more retentive than al-Darawardi. Abu al-Huwayrith's name is 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah."
"3414","3418 - Salamah ibn Shabib and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from 'Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3415","3419 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Abu Dawud informed us, saying: Abu 'Ubadah al-Ansari informed us, saying: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. Abu 'Ubadah said thus, not inserting anyone between al-Zuhri and Muhammad ibn Jubayr. Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' also followed him, saying: from al-Zuhri from Muhammad ibn Jubayr from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was distributing the spoils of Hunayn, when a samurah tree snatched his cloak. He said: O people, return my cloak to me; by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, were you to have gold to the number of its trees I would divide it among you, then you would not find me miserly nor cowardly. It is only the fifth, and the fifth is returned among you."
"3416","3420 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, saying: 'Abd al-Samad ibn al-Nu'man informed us, saying: Sa''ad ibn Sulayman informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it, adding in it: nor a liar - meaning: you will not find me miserly nor cowardly nor a liar. This hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Jubayr ibn Mut'im. Something like it was narrated from other than Jubayr."
"3417","3421 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali and 'Ali ibn Muslim informed us, saying: Abu Dawud informed us, saying: Abu 'Ubadah al-Ansari informed us, saying: al-Zuhri informed us, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Juhfah, and he said: Do you not bear witness that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and that the Qur'an came from Allah? We said: Yes indeed. He said: Then receive glad tidings, for this Qur'an - one end of it is in the Hand of Allah and the other end in your hands. Hold fast to it, for you will never perish nor go astray after it, ever. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except through this channel. Something like these words was narrated from other than Jubayr. We do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri except Abu 'Ubadah al-Ansari."
"3418","3422 - 'Abdullah ibn Shabib informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to me, saying: I found in my father's book, in his handwriting, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were around an idol of ours a month before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, having slaughtered a camel, when a crier cried out from its hollow: Hear the wonder - polytheism and filth have gone, and shooting stars were cast for a Prophet in Makkah named Ahmad, whose migration is to Yathrib. This hadith - we only mentioned it, though Jubayr ibn Mut'im mentioned nothing in it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we mentioned it because it was among the signs of his prophethood and mission. Everything a Companion narrated in which something is mentioned concerning the Prophet, even if he did not narrate it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we entered into the Musnad, since that speech is not retained from the Prophet from any channel."
"3419","3423 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Khalaf ibn Khalifah informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I lost a camel of mine and went seeking it at 'Arafah on the day of 'Arafah, when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: What is the matter with this one? He is of the Hums. Sufyan said: The Hums are Quraysh, who would not stand at 'Arafah."
"3420","3424 - Musa ibn 'Abdullah Abu Talhah al-Khuza'i informed us, saying: Bakr ibn Sulayman informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me, from 'Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his uncle Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before revelation was sent down upon him, while I was standing upon a camel of mine and he was standing upon a camel of his at 'Arafat with some people of his tribe, until he departed with them. This hadith has a sound chain. Something in this meaning was narrated from other than Jubayr ibn Mut'im with other than this wording. The hadith of Jubayr is firmer and more correct. The hadith of 'Amr ibn Dinar - we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Ibn 'Uyaynah. We do not know that 'Amr ibn Dinar narrated from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im from his father except two hadiths: this one, about which there is no disagreement, and the other, about which there is disagreement."
"3421","3425 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-'Uruqi informed us, saying: al-Salt ibn Muhammad Abu Hammam al-Kharaki informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let us go to Banu Waqif to visit al-Basir - a man who was blind. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it muttasil from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except Abu Hammam, who was trustworthy from Ibn 'Uyaynah. Abu Hammam contradicted others and was himself contradicted in its chain."
"3422","3426 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - without saying: from his father. Husayn al-Ju'fi contradicted him, narrating it from Ibn 'Uyaynah from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Let us go to Waqif. Thus Husayn said."
"3423","3427 - Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq informed us, saying: Husayn ibn 'Ali informed us, from Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir. We only mentioned this hadith despite the discrepancy and disturbance in its chain because we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a connected channel other than this, so we mentioned it and clarified the defect in it."
"3424","3428 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Abu Dawud informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3425","3429 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, saying: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. Abu Dawud said in his hadith: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The people of Yemen have come to you as though they are fragments of cloud, the best of the people of the earth. A man of the Ansar said: Except us? He said: Except you - a light word. Yazid ibn Harun said in his hadith from Ibn Abi Dhi'b from al-Harith from Muhammad ibn Jubayr from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey of his, and he said: The people of Yemen will come upon you as though they are the cloud; they are the best of those on earth. A man of the Ansar said: Except us? He fell silent, and he repeated it three times: Except us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A weak word: Except you. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel. We do not know for Jubayr ibn Mut'im a path other than this path."
"3426","3430 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa informed us, saying: Abu 'Amir informed us, saying: Zuhayr informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which lands are most beloved to Allah, and which lands are most hateful to Allah? He said: I do not know until I ask Jibril (peace be upon him). Jibril came to him and informed him that the most beloved places to Allah are the mosques, and the most hateful places to Allah are the markets. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except with this chain. 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil - the people accepted his hadith; we have explained what is due concerning his hadith elsewhere. These words were narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels, so we sufficed with the hadith of Jubayr, unless one of those who narrated that from the Messenger of Allah adds something, in which case we produce it for the sake of the addition. Ibn 'Aqil did not narrate from Muhammad ibn Jubayr other than this hadith."
"3427","3431 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, saying: my father informed us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq say: I heard Ya'qub ibn 'Utbah, and Jubayr ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from his grandfather. Thus Abu Musa, Bundar, and 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated it to us; all agreed upon this chain, because the copy of Wahb ibn Jarir from his father from Ibn Ishaq belonged to 'Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad, so it was in his book thus, and Abu Musa and Bundar copied from the book of 'Abd al-A'la, so it occurred in their books thus. [Isnad discussion only; matn follows in the next entry.]"
"3428","3432 - What is correct is what Salamah ibn Shabib and Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Waddah narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, saying: my father narrated to me, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from Ya'qub ibn 'Utbah, from Jubayr ibn Muhammad ibn Mut'im, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, souls are strained, dependents are lost, and wealth has perished; ask Allah for rain for us, for we seek your intercession with Allah, and we seek Allah's intercession with you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to you - do you know what you are saying? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) glorified Allah until that was recognized on his face and the faces of his Companions, and said: Woe to you - Allah is not interceded with before anyone; Allah is greater than that. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from any channel except this channel. Muhammad ibn Ishaq did not say in it: Ya'qub ibn 'Utbah narrated to me."
"3429","3433 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah informed us, saying: Husayn ibn Numayr informed us, saying: Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3430","3434 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi informed us of it, saying: Hushaym informed us, saying: Husayn informed us, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except through this channel. It was narrated from other than Jubayr. Hushaym differed with Husayn ibn Numayr; Hushaym is more retentive than Husayn ibn Numayr."
"3431","3435 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah informed us, saying: Husayn ibn Numayr informed us, from Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - one part over this mountain and one part over this mountain."
"3432","3436 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah informed us, saying: Abu Ja'far al-Razi informed us, from Husayn, from Jubayr ibn Muhammad ibn Jubayr, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he mentioned the like of it. This hadith - it was narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im through this channel which we mentioned. It was narrated from other than Jubayr with other than this wording. We only mentioned it because they differed from Husayn. Abu Ja'far al-Razi corroborated Ibrahim ibn Tahman in his narration and its continuity."
"3433","3437 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi informed us, saying: Abu Dawud informed us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. Abu Dawud said: In my view it is in one place from his father, and in one place not from his father: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned something to him, so he said to her: Come back to me. She said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I do not see you? He said: Go to Abu Bakr. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrates it except Jubayr ibn Mut'im from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a connected channel from him. We do not know that Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated a musnad hadith from Muhammad ibn Jubayr other than this hadith. Its chain is sound."
"3434","3438 - 'Abdullah ibn Shabib informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar al-Jubayri informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umayr informed us - thus I saw it with me in my book, and I deem him Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr - from Umayyah ibn Safwan, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays toward a sutrah, let him draw near to it, so that Satan does not interrupt his prayer. This hadith - we do not know anyone who said: from Muhammad ibn Jubayr from his father, other than Umayyah ibn Safwan. We do not retain it except through this channel."
"3435","3439 - al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, saying: 'Amr ibn Dinar informed us, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, descends to the heaven of this world and says: Is there any asker, that I may give him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness, that I may forgive him?"
"3436","3440 - Ahmad ibn Aban informed us of it, saying: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except through this channel. We do not know anyone who named the man other than Hammad ibn Salamah."
"3437","3441 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: 'Affan informed us, saying: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a military expedition, and they slept until the sun rose. He commanded Bilal, who called the adhan; then he commanded them and they prayed two rak'ahs, then he led them in the dawn prayer."
"3438","3442 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah and Ahmad ibn Aban informed us of it, saying: Sufyan informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. This hadith - we do not know for it a path from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except this path. We do not know anyone who narrated it naming after Nafi' ibn Jubayr except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"3439","3443 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Bukayr informed us, saying: Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us, from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the days of tashriq are for slaughter."
"3440","3444 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us of it, saying: 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us, saying: Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Tanukhi informed us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of 'Arafat is a standing place, but keep away from 'Uranah; all of Muzdalifah is a standing place, but keep away from Muhassir; all the passes of Mina are for sacrifice, and in all the days of tashriq there is slaughter. This hadith - we do not know anyone who said in it: from Nafi' ibn Jubayr from his father, except Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, who is a man not retentive and not adduced as proof when he is alone with a hadith. The hadith of Ibn Abi Husayn here is what is correct. Ibn Abi Husayn did not meet Jubayr ibn Mut'im. We only mentioned this hadith because we did not retain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: In all the days of tashriq there is slaughter, except in this hadith; for that reason we mentioned it and clarified the defect in it."
"3441","3445 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, saying: Shu'bah informed us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Asim al-'Anazi, from Ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father. [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3442","3446 - 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir informed us of it, saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, saying: Husayn informed us, from 'Amr ibn Murrah, from 'Abbad ibn 'Asim al-'Anazi, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he entered prayer, saying: Allah is Most Great, greatly; praise be to Allah, abundantly; glory be to Allah, morning and evening. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from Satan - from his hamz, his nafth, and his nafh. 'Amr ibn Murrah said: His hamz is madness, his nafh is pride - or arrogance - and his nafth is poetry. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Jubayr ibn Mut'im. We do not know for it a path except this path. They differed over the name of the 'Anazi who narrated it from Nafi' ibn Jubayr: Shu'bah said: from 'Amr from 'Asim al-'Anazi. Ibn Fudayl said: from Husayn from 'Amr from 'Abbad ibn 'Asim. Za'idah said: from Husayn from 'Amr from 'Ammar ibn 'Asim. The man is not known. We only mentioned it because none narrates these words from Nafi' ibn Jubayr from his father other than him, nor is it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from anyone else either."
"3443","3447 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi informed us, saying: Sulayman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi informed us, saying: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash informed us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydullah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord, the Mighty - three times - and in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High - three times. This hadith - it was narrated from other than Jubayr ibn Mut'im from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We do not know it narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except through this channel. 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Ubaydullah is fair in hadith but not strong; the scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"3444","3448 - al-'Abbas ibn Ja'far al-Baghdadi informed us, saying: Shabababah ibn Sawwar informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Qasim ibn 'Abbas, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: You blame me for arrogance, yet I have worn wool and led a goat by a rope - while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does that is free of pride. This hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Jubayr ibn Mut'im. We do not know for it a path from Jubayr except this path."
"3445","3449 - 'Amr ibn 'Ali informed us, saying: Abu Qutaybah informed us, saying: Qays informed us, from Mansur, from Kilab ibn 'Ali - and once he said: Qays informed us, from Mudrik ibn 'Ali, from Mansur ibn Abi Sulayman, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shorten his hair at al-Marwah with an arrowhead, then say: 'Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection. This hadith - we do not know for it a path from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except this path. It was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels that he said: 'Umrah has entered into Hajj. As for: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shorten his hair at al-Marwah with an arrowhead - we do not retain it except through this channel. Mudrik ibn 'Ali is unknown. Mansur ibn Abi Sulayman - we do not retain for him a musnad hadith. Kilab ibn 'Ali is a man of Kufah."
"3446","3450 - Abu Kurayb informed us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah informed us, saying: Isma'il ibn Muslim informed us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3447","3451 - Ahmad ibn 'Abdah informed us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from 'Abdullah ibn Babah, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3448","3452 - Yusuf ibn Musa informed us, saying: Jarir and Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from 'Abdullah ibn Babah, who said: I heard Jubayr ibn Mut'im (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Banu 'Abd Manaf - I shall certainly know if you withhold. In the hadith of Abu al-Zubayr from 'Abdullah ibn Babah from Jubayr he said: Do not prevent anyone who circumambulates this House at any hour he wills, by night or day, from praying. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel. We do not know it narrated from Jubayr ibn Mut'im except a weak hadith not established by transmission. In this hadith is an indication from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he permitted voluntary prayer after Fajr and after 'Asr in Makkah specifically, to the exclusion of elsewhere."
"3449","3453 - Salih ibn Mu'adh Abu Yunus informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn 'Umar ibn Waqid informed us, saying: Ishaq ibn Hazim informed us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade carrying out hudud punishments in the mosques. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a connected chain from a sound chain. This chain is among the best chains narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that, though the scholars spoke about Muhammad ibn 'Umar and weakened his hadith."
"3450","3454 - Yahya ibn Hakim informed us, saying: Safwan ibn 'Isa informed us, saying: Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Zuhri, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar (may Allah be pleased with him) informed us, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn moving among the people asking about the dwelling of Khalid ibn al-Walid. A drunkard was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded those with him to strike him with whatever was in their hands, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw dust upon him. Then Abu Bakr after him was brought a drunkard, and he aimed at their striking of him that day - or we aimed - striking forty. Then 'Umar struck forty. Thus I saw it in my book: he aimed at their striking of him."
"3451","3455 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah informed us, saying: 'Abd al-A'la informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn 'Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman and Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought one who had drunk, and he commanded that he be struck; they struck him with whatever was in their hands. In the time of Abu Bakr a drinker was brought, and he asked about his striking; we aimed at the striking with which we had struck the drinker in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), estimating it at forty, so he struck him forty. Then 'Umar struck eighty."
"3452","3456 - Muhammad ibn Miskin informed us, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam informed us, from Nafi' ibn Yazid, saying: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to me that 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Sa'ib informed him that 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar narrated from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The parable of the believer when fever or burning fever afflicts him is like a piece of iron that enters the fire - its dross goes and its good remains. This hadith - we do not know for it a path from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar except this path. The like of its words was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one channel with differing wordings. We only mentioned the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar because of the scarcity of his narration from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Sa'ib is known in lineage, except that he is not known for transmitting hadith. 'Abd al-Hamid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman - we do not know anyone who narrated from him except 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Sa'ib. The hadith of Abu Salamah and Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar - we only mentioned it because Abu Salamah and Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman did not narrate from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar other than this hadith. We do not know for 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar a chain better connected than this chain, though al-Zuhri met him. As for the hadith of Usamah from al-Zuhri from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar - others besides Usamah also narrated it, so we sufficed with Usamah."
"3453","3457 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl informed us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, saying: my father informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri - thus I retained it - from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that dust be thrown in their faces - meaning the praisers. This hadith - I deem it an omission by its transmitter; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw dust upon the drinker, but thus Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated it, and he was not corroborated in it."
"3454","3458 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' informed us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed us, from Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad, from his grandfather 'Abdullah ibn Hisham - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped over his head and supplicated for him while he was small - who said: 'Abdullah ibn Hisham used to sacrifice one sacrificial animal on behalf of all his household."
"3455","3459 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Junayd informed us, saying: Yahya ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bukayr informed us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Abu 'Aqil Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad, from his grandfather 'Abdullah ibn Hisham al-Qurashi al-Taymi (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was holding the hand of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. 'Umar said: By Allah, you, O Messenger of Allah, are more beloved to me than everything except myself. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No - by the One in Whose Hand is my soul - until I am more beloved to you than yourself. 'Umar said: Then you are now more beloved to me than myself. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now, O 'Umar. This hadith - we do not know it narrated except with this chain. We do not know anyone who narrates it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except 'Abdullah ibn Hisham. We do not know that 'Abdullah ibn Hisham narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except these two hadiths."
"3456","3460 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Isma'il narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Mustawrid (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you dipping his finger in the sea, then lifting it and looking at what comes out with it. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Mustawrid. A group narrated it from Isma'il, so we sufficed with the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah."
"3457","3461 - 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead sheep and said: The world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owners. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from al-Mustawrid except from the hadith of Mujalid from Qays from him. It was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one channel."
"3458","3462 - Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us, saying: 'Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Mujalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was sent at the onset of the Hour; I preceded it as this preceded this - pointing with his two fingers, the index and the middle. This hadith with this wording - we do not know it narrated except from al-Mustawrid from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The like of its words was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one channel with differing wordings. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Mujalid except 'Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad."
"3459","3463 - Muhammad ibn Rizqullah al-Kalwadhani narrated to us, saying: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, saying: Musa ibn 'Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad al-Fihri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The Hour will come while the Romans are the majority of people. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel with this chain."
"3460","3464 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Amr, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running his little finger between his toes when he performed ablution. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrates it with this wording except with this chain from al-Mustawrid. The like of its words was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from more than one channel with other than this wording."
"3461","3465 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Harithah ibn Wahb, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Hawd (Cistern), and al-Mustawrid said to him: Did you not hear him mention the vessels? He said: No. He said: But I heard him - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - say: Vessels are seen therein more numerous than the stars of the sky. This hadith from al-Mustawrid - we do not know for it a path other than this path, nor from Harithah ibn Wahb except through this channel. More than one narrated it from Shu'bah; the most eminent who narrated it from Shu'bah is Ibn Abi 'Adiyy."
"3462","3466 - Abu Kamil al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn al-Jahdari narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, saying: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3463","3467 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3464","3468 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Mansur, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, blessed and exalted, prescribed excellence upon everything; when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and give rest to his slaughtered animal. This hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Shaddad ibn Aws. A group narrated it from Khalid, among them those we named. Al-A'mash also narrated it from Khalid al-Hadhdha'. We do not know for it a path from Shaddad except: Khalid from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ash'ath from Shaddad."
"3465","3469 - al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, saying: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3466","3470 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from one who narrated to him, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3467","3471 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3468","3472 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, saying: Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Abu Ghifar al-Muthanna ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Abu Asma' al-Rahabi, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3469","3473 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, saying: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath, from Abu Asma', from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [Isnad-only entry; no matn given in the source text.]"
"3470","3474 - Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from 'Abdullah ibn Zayd, who is Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by a man being cupped on the seventeenth of Ramadan and said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast. This hadith - more than one narrated it from Khalid, so we sufficed with those we mentioned among them. As for the hadith of Ayyub: thus Ma'mar said - from Abu al-Ash'ath - while Isma'il is more retentive than Ma'mar. As for 'Asim and Abu Ghifar: they narrated it from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ash'ath from Abu Asma' from Shaddad. 'Asim is retentive, and Abu Ghifar is a shaykh from whom narration was taken. The hadith is the hadith of Khalid. As for the hadith of Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu Qilabah: we do not know anyone who narrated it musnad except Muhammad ibn Fudayl. We do not know that Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated from Abu Qilabah other than this hadith."
"3471","3475 - Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith al-Baghdadi informed us, saying: Shabababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the strap of one's sandal breaks, let him say: Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return - for it is among the calamities."
"3472","3476 - Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith informed us of it, saying: Shabababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, saying: Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, saying: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. The hadith of Khalid al-Hadhdha' which Kharijah narrated is the hadith of Shaddad ibn Aws. We do not know it narrated from Shaddad except through this channel. None narrated it from Khalid except Kharijah. I did not hear that anyone narrated it from Shabababah except Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith, who is a trustworthy, reliable man - though he was not corroborated in it. Kharijah ibn Mus'ab is not retentive."
"3473","3477 - Bishr ibn Dihyah al-Ziyadi narrated to us, saying: Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd al-Bahili narrated to us, from 'Asim ibn Makhlad, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from Shaddad ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever composes a verse of poetry after the last 'Isha' - his prayer of that night will not be accepted. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel. We do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Shaddad. It has no path from Shaddad except this path. 'Asim ibn Makhlad - we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd. Qaza'ah is a man of Basrah, unobjectionable, though not strong; the scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith. Yazid ibn Harun and others narrated this hadith from him."
"3474","3478 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, saying: 'Asim ibn Mihja' narrated to us, saying: Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Humayd al-A'raj, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud, from Shaddad ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you attend your dying, close the eyes - for sight follows the soul - and speak good, for the angels say amen to what the family of the deceased says. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Shaddad ibn Aws except through this channel. We do not know that Humayd al-A'raj narrated a musnad hadith from al-Zuhri except this hadith, and another hadith narrated by Ja'far ibn Sulayman from Humayd al-A'raj from al-Zuhri from 'Urwah from 'A'ishah - the hadith of al-Ifk. We do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd except Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd. We have already mentioned our note on Qaza'ah. It is al-Zuhri from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' - while in this hadith he said: from Mahmud ibn Labid. Al-Zuhri did not narrate from Mahmud ibn Labid."
"3475","3479 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Jurhah, from al-Zuhri, from Mahmud, from Shaddad ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not a liar who reconciles between people, conveying good or speaking good. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Shaddad ibn Aws from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain. Yahya ibn Jurhah - Ibn Jurayj and Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated from him. This hadith was only narrated by al-Zuhri from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from his mother Umm Kulthum."
"3476","3480 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, saying: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, saying: Hilal ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Abu Thabit Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Oppose the Jews and pray in your sandals, for they do not pray in their sandals nor in their khuffs. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Shaddad ibn Aws except through this channel with this chain."
"3477","3481 - 'Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We used to count minor shirk in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as ostentation. This hadith - we only mentioned it, though no speech from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is mentioned in it, because he said: in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We did not retain these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we mentioned it for that reason."
"3478","3482 - Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i narrated to us, saying: Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Shaddad ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays to show off has committed shirk, and whoever fasts to show off has committed shirk. This hadith with this wording - we do not know anyone who narrates it except Shaddad ibn Aws. We do not know for it a path except this path which we mentioned. 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram - a group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith. Shahr ibn Hawshab - Shu'bah spoke about him. We do not know anyone who abandoned narrating from him. Shu'bah narrated from a man from him. The meaning of: Whoever prays to show off has committed shirk, and whoever fasts to show off has committed shirk, is: prayer is for Allah, so when he shows it off to other than Him he has associated another in his deed which belongs to Allah; likewise fasting - it is only for Allah, so when he shows it off to a person it is as though he made the deed for Allah and for the person - not shirk in Allah."
"3479","3483 - 'Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Sakuni narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us, from Rashid ibn Dawud, from Ya'la ibn Shaddad ibn Aws, who said: My father Shaddad ibn Aws narrated to me, with 'Ubadah present confirming him, saying: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Is there any stranger among you - meaning the People of the Book? We said: No, O Messenger of Allah. He ordered the door closed and said: Raise your hands and say: There is no god but Allah. We raised our hands for a while. Then he said: O Allah, You sent me with this word, commanded me with it, promised me Paradise upon it, and You do not break the promise. Then he said: Receive glad tidings, for Allah has forgiven you. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except through this channel with this chain."
"3480","3484 - 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Himsi narrated to us, saying: 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to me, from al-Zubaydi, saying: al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me that Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to him, saying: Shaddad ibn Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, saying: We said: O Messenger of Allah, how were you taken by night on the night you were taken? He said: I led my Companions in the 'Atamah prayer in Makkah late at night. Jibril came to me with a white beast above a donkey and below a mule, saying: Ride. It proved difficult for me, so he turned it by its ear until it bore me upon it. It set off swooping with us, placing its hoof where its glance reached, until we ended at a land of palm trees. He said: Dismount. I dismounted. Then he said: Pray. I prayed, then we rode. He said to me: Do you know where you prayed? I said: Allah knows best. He said: You prayed at Yathrib; you prayed at Taybah. Then it set off swooping with us, placing its hoof where its glance reached, until we reached a white land. He said to me: Dismount. I dismounted. Then he said to me: Pray. I prayed, then we rode. He said: Do you know where you prayed? I said: Allah knows best. He said: You prayed at Madyan; you prayed by the tree of Musa. Then it set off swooping with us, placing its hoof - or its hoof falls - where its glance reached. Then we ascended. He said: Dismount. I dismounted. He said: Pray. I prayed, then we rode. He said to me: Do you know where you prayed? I said: Allah knows best. He said: You prayed at Bayt Lahm, where the Messiah 'Isa son of Maryam was born. Then he took me until we entered the City through its eighth gate. He brought his beast to the qiblah of the mosque and tied it, and we entered the mosque through a gate in which the sun and the moon incline. I prayed in the mosque where Allah willed - thus Ibn Zabraq said. Then I was brought two vessels, in one milk and in the other honey, both sent to me together. I weighed between them, then Allah guided me to it and I took the milk and drank until it struck my forehead. Before me was an old man reclining, who said: Your companion has taken the fitrah - or said: with the fitrah. Then he took me until we came to the valley that is at the City, when Hell was uncovered like a mat. We said: O Messenger of Allah, how did you find it? He said: Like - and he mentioned something that escaped me. Then we passed by a caravan of Quraysh at such-and-such place, who had lost a camel of theirs. I greeted them. One of them said: This is the voice of Muhammad. Then I came to my Companions before dawn in Makkah. Abu Bakr came to me and said: O Messenger of Allah, where were you tonight? I missed you in your place. He said: I came to Bayt al-Maqdis tonight. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a month's journey - describe it to me. A latch was opened for me as though I were looking at it; they asked me about nothing but I informed them of it. Abu Bakr said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. The polytheists said: Look at Abu Kabshah - he claims he came to Bayt al-Maqdis tonight. He said: Yes, and I passed by a caravan of yours at such-and-such place, who had lost a camel of theirs at such-and-such place. I am guiding them to you: they will alight at such-and-such, then come to you on such-and-such day, led by a dusky camel upon which is a black saddle-cloth and two black sacks. When that day came, the people looked out until near midday, when the caravan approached, led by that camel as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had described. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Shaddad ibn Aws from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"3481","3485 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari, and Abdah ibn Abd Allah al-Qasmali, and Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratisisi narrated to us, they said: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani, from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the best of your days is Friday; on it Adam was created, on it he was taken, and on it is the Blast, so send much blessings upon me on it, for your blessings are presented to me. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how will they be presented to you when you have decayed? He said: They say: you have perished. He said: Indeed Allah has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the Prophets. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone narrating it except Shaddad ibn Aws, and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain from Shaddad, and none narrated it except Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi. And it is said: this Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid is Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim, but the people of Kufah, Abu Usamah and al-Husayn al-Jufi, erred in it, although we do not know Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim narrating from Abu al-Ashath; they only said that because Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir is trustworthy, while Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Tamim is weak in hadith, and this hadith contained objectionable speech from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: it is more like that of Abd al-Rahman ibn Tamim."
"3482","3486 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said: Rashid ibn Dawud al-Sanani narrated to us, from Abu Asma, from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There will be after me leaders who will kill the prayer from its times, so pray the prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them as supererogatory. And when al-Hajjaj came, he delayed the prayer from its times, so I used to pray the prayer at its time and make my prayer with them supererogatory. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Shaddad except from this channel, and part of its wording is narrated from other than Shaddad from the Prophet from other channels."
"3483","3487 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ashath, from Abu Asma, from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, folded the earth for me until I saw its easts and its wests, and the dominion of my ummah will reach what was folded for me of it, and my Lord gave me the two treasures, the red and the white, and I asked my Lord not to destroy it by a general famine, nor to grant mastery over it to an enemy so they perish by a general destruction, nor to clothe us in factions, nor to make us taste the violence of one another. So He said: O Muhammad, when I decree a decree it is not repelled, and I have granted you for your ummah that I will not destroy them by a general famine, nor grant mastery over them to an enemy so they destroy them by a general destruction, until some of them kill others and some of them enslave others. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I fear for my ummah only the misguiding leaders, and when the sword is placed in my ummah it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection. Ahmad ibn Mansur said: So I said to Abd al-Razzaq: This is only from Thawban. He said: No, you have considered, and it is like this. And this hadith was narrated by Hammad ibn Zayd, and Abbad ibn Mansur, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that is the correct. And Qatadah narrated it from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Asma, from Thawban, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3484","3488 - Abu Kamil, and Ahmad ibn Malik narrated to us, and the wording is Ahmad's, they said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Bushayr ibn Kab, from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The chief of seeking forgiveness, when one of you turns from his prayer, is that he says: O Allah, You created me and I am Your servant, I am upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I can; I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I did; I acknowledge Your blessing upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Shaddad ibn Aws, and this isnad is among the best isnads narrated from Shaddad and the most connected from him."
"3485","3489 - And Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Damrah ibn Habib, from Shaddad ibn Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The intelligent is the one who subdued his soul and worked for what is after death, and the incapable is the one who made his soul follow its desire and wished upon Allah. And this speech, we do not know it narrated except from Shaddad ibn Aws from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain."
"3486","Musnad of Iyad ibn Himar, may Allah be pleased with him. What Iyad ibn Himar narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 3490 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hammam, meaning Ibn Yahya, narrated to us, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, he said: Four narrated to me from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, among them Yazid ibn Abd Allah, the brother of Mutarrif, and al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi, and two men whom Hammam forgot, from Iyad ibn Himar."
"3487","3491 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Four narrated to me from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, among them Yazid ibn Abd Allah and al-Ala ibn Ziyad, and two men whom Hammam forgot, from Iyad ibn Himar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivering a sermon, saying in his sermon: Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to teach you what you were ignorant of, of what He taught me this day of mine. Indeed all wealth that I have granted My servants is lawful, and I created My servants all as upright, and the devils came to them and diverted them from their religion and forbade for them what I had made lawful for them, and commanded them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. And indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, looked at the people of the earth and abhorred them, their Arabs and their non-Arabs, except remnants of the People of the Book. So He said: O Muhammad, I only sent you to test you and to test by you, and I sent down upon you a Book that water does not wash away, you recite it sleeping and awake. And indeed my Lord, the Blessed and Exalted, commanded me to burn Quraysh, so I said: O Lord, then they will crush my head and leave it like bread. He said: Expel them as they expelled you, and spend, it will be spent upon you, and send an army, I will send five like them, and fight with those who obey you those who disobey you. And He said: The companions of Paradise are three: a just, truthful, guided possessor of authority, and a man soft-hearted to every Muslim, and a chaste, charitable man. And He said: The companions of the Fire are five: a man whose greed is not hidden but he betrays it, and a man who neither evenings nor mornings except while deceiving you about your family and your wealth, and the weak who has no restraint, those among you who are followers. So a man said: O Abu Abd Allah, is he from the clients or from the Arabs? He said: He is the follower, who follows a man and obtains from his service illicitly without marriage. He said: And he mentioned miserliness and lying, or he said: lying and miserliness. And this hadith was narrated by Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Iyad, so we did not mention it, because in the hadith of Said, Yazid ibn Abd Allah and al-Ala were omitted, and Qatadah did not hear it from Mutarrif, so we mentioned it from Hammam since he had connected it, and Awf corroborated him in his narration, from Hakim al-Athram, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from Iyad."
"3488","3492 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated it to us with it, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Hakim al-Athram, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And Hakim al-Athram is Basran; Awf and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from him, but in his hadith there is something, because Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from him an objectionable hadith, so for that we began with the hadith of Qatadah before it, and were it not for that we would have mentioned al-Hasan from Mutarrif since he was more eminent."
"3489","3493 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Iyad ibn Himar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two who revile each other are two devils disputing abusively and lying to each other."
"3490","3494 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Iyad ibn Himar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a milch she-camel while he was a polytheist, so he returned it, and said: We have been forbidden the aid of the polytheists, meaning their support. And these two hadiths were narrated by Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Iyad ibn Himar, while Imran said: from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Iyad. And I think that Yazid ibn Abd Allah only heard it from Mutarrif."
"3491","3495 - And Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Said al-Darimi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father, from Matar, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Iyad ibn Himar, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Indeed Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, revealed to me that you be humble, so that no one boasts over another. And the hadiths of Iyad ibn Himar, we do not know anyone narrating them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) other than him."
"3492","Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him. Hadith of Abd Allah ibn Busr from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). 3496 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abd Allah ibn Busr al-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by my father while he was upon a white mule, so he took its bridle. He said: O Messenger of Allah, alight with us. So he alighted with him, and he brought him hays, and he ate, then he brought him dates, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began eating, and saying with the date-stones like this, and Shubah joined his two fingers. He said: Then drink was brought, so he drank, then he passed to the one on his right, then he said: O Allah, bless for them in what You have provided them, forgive them and have mercy on them."
"3493","3497 - And Yahya ibn Hakim narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shubah, from Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"3494","3498 - And Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, so my mother threw for him a blanket and he sat upon it, and she brought him dates, so he began eating and saying with the date-stones like this, and he described that he used to cast it from his mouth upon the back of his two fingers, the middle and the index, then turn the index upon the middle and throw the stone from its top. Then he called for drink, so he drank and passed to the one on his right, then he said: O Allah, bless for them in what You have provided them, forgive them and have mercy on them."
"3495","3499 - al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Rukhami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not come to houses from their doors, but come to them from their sides, then greet, and if permission is given to you then enter, otherwise return."
"3496","3500 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you know those of your ummah whom you have not seen? He said: Radiant from the traces of wudu."
"3497","3501 - And Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr. Abu Bakr said: And I saw it in my book in another place."
"3498","3502 - Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Tai narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: You will certainly reach a generation. He said: So it reached us that a hundred years passed over him."
"3499","3503 - Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: Hariz ibn Uthman al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Abd Allah ibn Busr and he had companionship, so I said to him among my companions: Did you see the Messenger of Allah as an old man? He said: So he placed his hand upon his tuft, and said: There were white hairs here."
"3500","3504 - And Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hariz ibn Uthman informed us, he said: I said to Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him: Was the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) an old man? He said: There were white hairs in the front of his beard, and he pointed to the front of his beard."
"3501","3505 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Ibn Abi Bilal, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between the great battle and the conquest of the city are six years, and the emergence of the Dajjal is in the seventh."
"3502","3506 - Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon on Friday when a man came, so he said to him: Sit, for you have harmed and delayed."
"3503","3507 - And Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Janah, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted Abu Bakr and Umar about a matter he intended, so they said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So he said: Call Muawiyah for me. And when he stood before him he said: Make him witness your affair, make him present your affair, for he is strong and trustworthy."
"3504","3508 - Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, from his father, Uthman ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsibi, from Abd Allah ibn Busr, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glad tidings to whoever finds in his record much seeking of forgiveness."
"3505","Musnad of Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him. First hadith of Imran ibn Husayn. 3509 - Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar informed us, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu Salih narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The standing of one of you in the row for an hour is better than the worship of one of them for sixty years. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it with this wording except Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain better than this chain with this speech, and we do not know anyone narrating this hadith from Yahya ibn Ayyub except Abu Salih, nor narrating it from Hisham ibn Hassan except Yahya ibn Ayyub, and we do not know it narrated nor known from the hadith of Hisham ibn Hassan. And Yahya ibn Ayyub is trustworthy, and Abu Salih, the people of knowledge narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"3506","3510 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while he disliked three tribes: Banu Umayyah, and Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran ibn Husayn and other than Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know anyone narrating this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abd al-Qahir ibn Shuayb, and there is no harm in him, and Rawh ibn Ubadah. And it has been narrated from Imran from another channel, and this isnad is the best isnad narrated in that from Imran."
"3507","3511 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Imran narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran from other channels, so we mentioned this hadith from this channel from Imran because it was the rarest outlet narrated in that from Imran. And we do not know anyone narrating this hadith from Simak except Hafs ibn Imran, and he is a man of Kufah, and we do not know anyone narrating it from Hafs except Ismail ibn Aban, and he is a man who inclines to Shiism, and the people of knowledge narrated from him and accepted his hadith. And we do not know Simak narrating, from al-Hasan, from Imran, except two hadiths, this is one of them, and it is strange, and the other is well-known."
"3508","3512 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to walk barefoot and shod, and drink standing and sitting, and turn from his right and his left, and fast while traveling and break fast. And this speech was narrated by Husayn al-Muallim, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Harun said: from Husayn, from Ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn. And there is no harm in Harun, and Harun added in his hadith: he fasts while traveling and breaks fast. And we did not retain this from the hadith of Amr ibn Shuayb, and had we retained it, this isnad would have been better than that, though that is the well-known."
"3509","3513 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn al-Muallim informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of one sitting is upon half of the prayer of one standing, and the prayer of one sleeping is upon half of the prayer of one sitting. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer of one sleeping upon half of the prayer of one sitting except in this hadith. Rather it is only narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various channels about the prayer of one sitting upon half of the prayer of one standing. And its isnad is good."
"3510","3514 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Muallim narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) warned us of every eloquent hypocrite. And this speech, we only retain it from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and they differed about raising it from Umar, so we mentioned it from Imran since there was disagreement about raising it from Umar. And the isnad of Umar is a sound isnad, so we brought it out from Umar, and repeated it from Imran due to the goodness of the isnad of Imran."
"3511","3515 - Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Ibn Buraydah, from Imran, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I had piles, so I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Pray sitting, and if you cannot then upon the side. And this speech, we do not retain it about the description of prayer according to human capacity from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel, and we do not know for it any chain from Imran except this chain. And its isnad is good, and more than one narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, so we sufficed with whom we mentioned apart from others."
"3512","3516 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him or to a man: Have you fasted anything of the end of this month? He said: No. He said: So when you break fast of Ramadan, then fast two days. And this speech, we do not know it narrated except from Imran from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it has been narrated from him through various chains, so we mentioned this chain of them since it was of good isnad, and there was in it explanation of the end days, since he said to him: When you break fast of the month of Ramadan, then fast two days, a proof that the end days are at its beginning."
"3513","3517 - al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization, so we were cauterized and we neither prospered nor succeeded. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Imran alone, and it has isnads from Imran, so we sufficed with this channel of them apart from others, unless another adds speech in that, then it is written for the sake of the addition in it."
"3514","3518 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursing the believer is like killing him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Imran and from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, so we mentioned the hadith of Imran due to the goodness of its isnad, and because Imran is greater in eminence. And we do not know anyone narrating this hadith except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"3515","3519 - Yahya ibn Muhammad, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil narrated to us, they said: Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man says to his brother: O disbeliever, then it is like killing him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Imran ibn Husayn with this wording and from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak, so we mentioned the hadith of Imran due to his eminence. And we do not know anyone narrating the hadith of Imran saying: from Imran, except Hammad ibn Salamah. And we do not know anyone narrating these two hadiths upon what we mentioned of their two isnads, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran, except Ishaq ibn Idris from Hammad ibn Salamah. And Ishaq, there was no harm in him, except that he narrated hadiths not corroborated upon."
"3516","3520 - Yahya ibn Muhammad, and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever kills himself with something in this world will be punished with it in the Hereafter. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from anyone with this wording with an isnad better than this isnad from Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain from Imran ibn Husayn except this chain. And some of those who narrated it said: from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Thabit ibn al-Dahhak."
"3517","3521 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them. And Allah knows whether he mentioned the third or said: And there will arise a people who bear witness and are not asked to bear witness; obesity will spread among them. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to its speech but not its wording, and it was narrated from Imran also that from other channels, and this isnad is the best isnad narrated in that from Imran with this wording."
"3518","3522 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, he said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined between Hajj and Umrah, and did not forbid it, nor did a book descend forbidding it, and that he said: He used to greet me until I was cauterized, and when I was cauterized the greeting upon me ceased. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran from other channels, so we sufficed with this channel of them apart from others."
"3519","3523 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If you have fasted anything of the end of this month, otherwise, when the people break fast, then fast two days, meaning when the people break fast of the month of Ramadan. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran ibn Husayn from other channels, and we already mentioned a channel before this, and in this hadith he mentioned a word other than what he mentioned in the hadith of Thabit, so we mentioned it for that, though the meaning is one."
"3520","3524 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will not cease a party of my ummah upon the truth, manifest, fighting those who oppose them. Mutarrif said: They are the people of Sham. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from other channels, so we mentioned the hadith of Imran ibn Husayn, and sufficed with it, unless another than Imran comes from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it with something adding, then it is written due to the addition."
"3521","3525 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Awn ibn Abi Shaddad al-Uqayli narrated to me, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, forgive me what I erred, and what I concealed, and what I declared, and what I was ignorant of, and what I did deliberately. And this hadith is not retained with this wording except from Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any isnad from Imran ibn Husayn except this isnad, and we do not know anyone narrating it except Muadh ibn Hisham alone."
"3522","3526 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Salman al-Makki narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Imran ibn al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The standing of a man in a row in the path of Allah is better than his worship in his house for sixty years."
"3523","3527 - Ubayd ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of my ummah is like rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with an isnad better than this isnad, and we do not know it narrated from Imran ibn Husayn except from this channel, except that Ismail ibn Nasr was alone with this hadith and none corroborated him upon it."
"3524","3528 - Amr ibn Ali, and Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man freed six slaves of his at death, he had no wealth other than them, so he freed them at his death, so that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he divided them into three parts; he freed two and enslaved four."
"3525","3529 - Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3526","3530 - And Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran ibn Husayn from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various channels and from other than Imran ibn Husayn. And its isnad is good. And in it is of jurisprudence that it is not permitted for a man to bequeath more than a third, for if he bequeaths more than a third it is rejected, because the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the whole to a third. And in it is that the sick man has no right to dispose of his wealth when his illness intensifies and is feared upon him except a third, for if he gives out more than a third it is returned, even if it was not his bequest, for it is in the position of a bequest."
"3527","3531 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, so they camped and slept, and did not wake until the sun rose. And when it rose, he commanded them and they prayed. And this hadith is narrated from Imran and others, and we do not know for Imran a chain better than this chain, because Yunus ibn Ubayd made its isnad good."
"3528","3532 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: When Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came to Basrah and prayed with them, he used to say takbir whenever he rose and lowered, so Imran said: This shaykh reminded us of a prayer we used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3529","3533 - Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And this hadith, we mentioned it from Yunus, though it is not connected, due to the eminence of Yunus, and because this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from Yunus except al-Mutamir, so for that we mentioned. As for the hadith of al-Jurayri, then it is connected. And Abu al-Ala is Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, and he is the brother of Mutarrif. And this speech has been narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from other channels, and Imran is the highest who narrated that from a sound channel."
"3530","3534 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Humran narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from Qatadah except Said, and we do not know anyone narrating it from Said except Amr ibn Humran. And there was no harm in him. And similar to its speech has been narrated from Imran from other channels with different wordings."
"3531","3535 - Ismail ibn Masud narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jallab, nor janab, nor shighar in Islam, and whoever plunders is not of us. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Imran ibn Husayn with this wording with better than this isnad from Imran."
"3532","3536 - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We performed tamattu on the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no prohibition descended about us, nor did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran ibn Husayn from various channels with different wordings. And this isnad is the best by which it is narrated with this wording from Imran."
"3533","3537 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good."
"3534","3538 - And al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran from various channels, and this isnad is the best by which it is narrated in that. And the hadith of Hammad from Humayd, we do not know anyone narrating it from Hammad except Habban ibn Hilal, and he is trustworthy, reliable in what he narrates."
"3535","3539 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plundering."
"3536","3540 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization."
"3537","3541 - Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran from other channels, and we do not know it narrated except from Imran ibn Husayn, and its isnad is good. And Ali ibn Asim said in it: from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from Imran."
"3538","3542 - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, raising it, he said: Whoever aids his brother while he is able to aid him, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter."
"3539","3543 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, he did not raise it."
"3540","3544 - And Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ufrah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids his brother in absence while he is able to aid him, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter. And this speech, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with an isnad better than this isnad, and we do not know it narrated except from Imran ibn Husayn alone with this isnad. And more than one narrated it from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran, halted."
"3541","3545 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon him a man, and in his hand was a ring of brass, so he said: What is this? He said: It was described to me for weakness. He said: Cast it from you; do you love to be entrusted to it. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-Hasan, from Imran, and we do not know it narrated from the hadith of Yunus, from al-Hasan, except from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, and we did not hear it except from Amr."
"3542","3546 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3543","3547 - And Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Habban narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and in my hands was a ring of brass, so he said: What is this doing in your hand? I said: For weakness. He said: Do you love to be entrusted to it; cast it from you. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Imran ibn Husayn alone, and we do not know anyone narrating it from Imran except al-Hasan, and a group narrated it from al-Hasan."
"3544","3548 - Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Bashir ibn Jahl narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning going in the path of Allah or an evening going is better than the world and what is in it. And this speech was narrated by a group from al-Hasan, from Imran, and we do not know from Imran any chain other than this chain. And Salm ibn Bashir is Basran, there is no harm in him."
"3545","3549 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us, from Matar, or Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not ride purple, nor wear qassi, nor wear a shirt bordered with silk. Indeed the perfume of men is scent with no color, indeed the perfume of women is color with no scent. And this speech, we do not know it narrated except from Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor narrating it from Imran, except al-Hasan."
"3546","3550 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: And you see the people drunk, while they are not drunk. And this speech, we do not know it narrated except from Imran ibn Husayn; we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) other than him, and we do not know for it any chain from him other than this chain. al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik abridged it, and mentioned the recitation in it, so it became a hadith by itself. And al-Hakam is not strong, except that more than one narrated from him."
"3547","3551 - Amr ibn Ali, and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Affan, and Abu Dawud narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My son's son died, so what is for me of his inheritance? He said: For you is a sixth. And when he turned, he called him and said: For you is a sixth. And when he turned, he called him and said: The other sixth is additional food. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel with this isnad from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3548","3552 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Habban narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from Imran ibn Husayn except Hammam, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran. And Yunus narrated it from al-Hasan, from Imran, so we mentioned the hadith of Imran from the hadith of Qatadah due to his differing in its isnad."
"3549","3553 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Mansur narrated to us, from Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We were with him in Basrah, so we passed by a man reciting Surah Yusuf. He said: So he sat and said to us: Listen to the Quran. And when the reciter finished his recitation, he asked. So Imran said: Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. Then Imran said to us: Go, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever of you recites the Quran, let him ask Allah by it, for there will come peoples after you asking people by it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Imran, and we do not know anyone narrating it from Imran except al-Hasan, nor from al-Hasan except Khaythamah, and he is Khaythamah ibn Abi Khaythamah, a man of Basrah; Mansur narrated from him. And Qabisah narrated this hadith from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, from Imran, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3550","3554 - al-Sakan ibn Said narrated it to us with it, from Qabisah, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Khaythamah, from al-Hasan, from Imran, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"3551","3555 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Madan narrated to us, from Imran al-Qasir, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Qalus, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I have not narrated to anyone since I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), fearing people would rely upon it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever knows that Allah is his Lord and that I am His Prophet, certain from his heart, and he pointed with his hand to his skin, Allah will forbid him to the Fire, or Allah will forbid his skin to the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain from Imran except this chain. And Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Qalus is Basran, and Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Madan is Basran, there is no harm in him."
"3552","3556 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a she-camel of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was lost, and a woman vowed to slaughter it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow upon anyone in disobedience, or he forbade vowing in disobedience. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it except Imran with this wording, and its isnad is good."
"3553","3557 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Are the people of Paradise known from the people of Fire? He said: Yes. They said: Then for what is action? He said: Act, or he said: Each acts for what he was created for. Shubah said: For what he was created for, or for what was made easy for him. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran ibn Husayn from other channels, so we mentioned this hadith of them with this hadith, and sufficed with this chain from Imran, and did not repeat it from others, unless another adds something in it, then we write it for the sake of the addition."
"3554","3558 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Yazid al-Rishk narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment and appointed Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"3555","3559 - al-Qasim ibn Wahb al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Mindal narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There is no vow in disobedience."
"3556","3560 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3557","3561 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Hanzali narrated to us, from his father, from a man, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Imran except from the hadith of Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, and there was disagreement from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr. And Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, his hadith was only weakened due to this hadith by Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid."
"3558","3562 - Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"3559","3563 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn Muhabbab narrated to us, he said: Jisr ibn Farqad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, the nephew of al-Hasan, from al-Hasan, he said: I met Imran ibn Husayn and Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with them, so I asked them about the interpretation of this verse: And good dwellings in gardens of Eden. They said: You have come upon the expert; we asked about it the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: A palace of pearl, in that palace seventy thousand houses of green emerald, in every house of them seventy beds, upon every bed seventy beddings of every color, upon every bedding a woman of the wide-eyed maidens, in every house seventy tables, upon every table seventy kinds, in every house seventy servants or maidservants; he is given of strength what covers all that in one morning. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Imran ibn Husayn and Abu Hurayrah, and we do not know for them any chain narrated from them except this chain. And Jisr ibn Farqad is weak in hadith, and the people of knowledge narrated from him and narrated from him. And al-Hasan, his hearing from Abu Hurayrah is not sound from the narration of the trustworthy, from al-Hasan."
"3560","3564 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We journeyed by night with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a battle, and when it was predawn we camped, and nothing woke us except the heat of the sun. So a man began waking startled, frightened. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride. So he rode and we rode until the sun rose. So he alighted and commanded Bilal, and he called, so we prayed the two rakahs before the morning, then he established and prayed with us. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not make it up at its time tomorrow? So he said: No, Allah forbids you usury and accepts it from you. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it with this wording except Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain from Imran except this chain. And similar to its speech and its meaning has been narrated from various channels with different wordings, so we mentioned every hadith with its wording in its place."
"3561","3565 - And Abdah ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning; they are those who do not cauterize, nor seek ruqyah, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from Hisham, from al-Hasan, from Imran, except Yazid ibn Harun. And other than Yazid narrated it from Hisham, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran. And Imran ibn al-Husayn narrates this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Masud in much speech, this is its end, so we mentioned the hadith of Abd Allah in full in its place. And I think Imran ibn Husayn only abridged from him, al-Hasan abridged this hadith in the narration of Hisham ibn Hassan from him."
"3562","3566 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us. 3567 - And Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Harb narrated to us, from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz, from Kathir ibn Shinzhir, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation, and that among mutilation is that a man performs Hajj walking or shaves his head. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from any of the channels except Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain from Imran except this chain. And Abu Amir al-Khazzaz is trustworthy, and Kathir ibn Shinzhir, there is no harm in him; Hammad ibn Zayd and others narrated from him."
"3563","3568 - Husayn ibn Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Zadham narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wailing. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from Imran with better than this isnad. And Shubah narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Subayh, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3564","3569 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar informed us of it, from Ghundar. 3570 - al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur. 3571 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good."
"3565","3572 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The asking of the rich is a blemish on his face, and the asking of the rich is fire; if given little, then little, and if given much, then much. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from Imran ibn Husayn. And similar to its meaning has been narrated from other than Imran ibn Husayn without its wording, so we mentioned it in its place. And Ismail ibn Muslim is not strong, and al-Amash and al-Thawri and many people of knowledge narrated from him."
"3566","3573 - Raja ibn Muhammad al-Saqati narrated to us, he said: A man narrated to us, he named him, his name slipped from me, he said: Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, from his father, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is called to a judge among the judges of the Muslims and does not come to him, then he is unjust, or he said: he has no right. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet, upon him prayer and peace, connected in isnad, except from this channel from Imran ibn Husayn. And more than one narrated it from al-Hasan, disconnected. And Rawh ibn Ata made it connected from his father. And Rawh is weak in hadith, and Ata is well-known Basran; Khalid al-Hadhdha and Shubah and others narrated from him."
"3567","3574 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi, and Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, they said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal has certainly eaten food and walked in the markets. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a channel better than this channel, although there was disagreement in it from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ibn Uyaynah. So a group said: from Ibn Uyaynah, from Ali, from al-Hasan ibn Imran. And more than one of the companions of Ibn Uyaynah said: from Ali, from al-Hasan, from Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal. And I think Ibn Uyaynah narrated it like this once, and once narrated it like this. And Hammad ibn Salamah said: from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not mention Imran nor Abd Allah ibn Mughaffal."
"3568","3575 - Abd Allah ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet."
"3569","3576 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, that peoples came to Imran ibn Husayn and said: Do not narrate to us except what is in the Book of Allah. So he became angry, and said: From where do you find in the Book of Allah the five prayers, and in every two hundred five dirhams, and in every forty dinars a dinar, and in every twenty half a dinar, things of this he enumerated, but take as we took. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from al-Hasan, from Imran, except Ali ibn Zayd. And there was disagreement from Ali, so some said: from Abu Nadrah, and some said: from al-Hasan."
"3570","3577 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shayban said: Khalid ibn Jamil informed me, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The supplication of a brother for his brother in absence is not rejected. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Imran ibn Husayn except from this channel with this isnad. And Khalid ibn Jamil is Basran."
"3571","3578 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who takes omens or has omens taken for him, or practices soothsaying or has it practiced for him, or practices magic or has it practiced for him. And whoever ties a knot, or he said: whoever ties a knot, and whoever comes to a soothsayer and believes him in what he says, then he has disbelieved in what was sent down upon Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, part of its speech has been narrated from other channels, but as for with all its speech and its wording, then we do not know it narrated except from Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain from Imran ibn Husayn except this chain. And Abu Hamzah al-Attar is Basran, there is no harm in him."
"3572","3579 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub, and al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, they said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Shabib ibn Shaybah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3573","3580 - And Abu Said Abd Allah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Imran ibn Husayn, and the wording is Shabib ibn Shaybah's, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to my father: O Husayn, how many gods do you worship today? He said: Seven, six on earth and one in heaven. He said: Which of them do you count for your hope and your fear? He said: The One in heaven. So he said: O Husayn, if you become Muslim I will teach you two words that will benefit you. And when Husayn became Muslim, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me what you promised me. He said: Say: O Allah, inspire me my right guidance and protect me from the evil of my soul. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Imran ibn Husayn and his father. And they differed in its isnad, so Ribi ibn Hirash said: from Imran ibn Husayn, from his father. And al-Hasan and al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Rahman said: from Imran, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Husayn. And I think the hadith of Imran, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his father, is more correct."
"3574","3581 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq, and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, and al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari, may Allah be pleased with them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with better than this isnad."
"3575","3582 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I looked into the Fire, and most of its people were women. And this hadith, they differed in it, so more than one narrated it from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas. And more than one narrated it from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn. And its isnad is good."
"3576","3583 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your brother, al-Najashi, has died, so pray over him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone saying in it, from Muhammad, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Imran, except Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, and he is trustworthy, from Yunus ibn Ubayd. And this speech and this act has been narrated from Imran from various channels, and this isnad is the best of them as a chain from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3577","3584 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Awf narrated to us, he said: Abu Raja narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and we journeyed one night until we were at the end of the night, we fell that fall, and there is no fall sweeter to the traveler than it. So nothing woke us except the heat of the sun. So the first to wake was so-and-so, then so-and-so, he used to name them, and Umar ibn al-Khattab was the fourth. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he slept was not woken until he was the one who woke. We did not know what happens or happens to him in his sleep. And when he woke, he saw what befell the people, and he was a hollow man, meaning Umar. He said: So he said takbir and raised his voice with takbir. He said: So he kept saying takbir and raising his voice until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke by his voice. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke, they complained to him what befell them, so he said: No harm, or: it will not harm; ride. So he went and alighted not far, and we alighted. So he called for water for wudu, and performed wudu, and the call was made for prayer, so he prayed with the people. And when he turned from his prayer, there was a man apart who had not prayed with the people. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, janabah befell me and there is no water. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is the earth, for it suffices you. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went, so the people complained to him of thirst. So he alighted, then he called so-and-so, Abu Raja naming him, and Awf forgetting him, and called Ali, so he said: Go and seek water, or: seek for us water. He said: So they went. He said: So they met a woman between two waterskins, or two spreads, of water upon her camel. So they said to her: When was your covenant with water? She said: My covenant was yesterday this hour, and our people are absent. So they said to her: Go. She said: To where? So they said to her: To the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So she said: To this who is called the Sabian. So they said: He is the one you mean, so go to him. So they brought her to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she narrated to him the account. So they made her alight from her camel, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel, so he poured in it from the mouths of the two waterskins or the two spreads, then tied their mouths and released the outlets. And it was called among the people that they water, so whoever watered, watered, and whoever gave to drink, gave to drink. And the last of that was that he gave the one whom janabah had befallen a vessel of water, so he said: Go and pour it upon you. And she was standing looking at what was done with her water. He said: By Allah, it was lifted from her when it was lifted, and it appears to me that it was fuller than when he watered it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather for her. So they gathered for her between dates and flour and parched barley; so they gathered much food, and made it in a cloth, and carried it upon her camel, and placed the cloth before her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Know, by Allah, we did not diminish anything of your water, but Allah is Who gave us to drink. He said: So she came to her people, having been detained from them, so they said: What detained you, O so-and-so? She said: Wonder; two men met me and took me to this who is called the Sabian, so he did with my water such-and-such. By Allah, he is either the most magician between this and this, pointing her middle and index fingers, and she raised them to the sky, meaning between the heaven and the earth, or he is indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So the people used to raid and raid those around her and not raid her. So she said one day to her people: What do you see, the people raid and raid those around you and do not raid you. So they came and entered into Islam."
"3578","3585 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Peoples will exit the Fire by the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), called the Jahannamiyyun. And this hadith has been narrated from various channels from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this is among the good channels narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Safwan said in it: from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan, there is no harm in him; Yahya ibn Said and Safwan and a group narrated from him."
"3579","3586 - Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to it."
"3580","3587 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Imran Abu Bakr narrated to us, he said: Abu Raja al-Utaridi narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and no book descended about us, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid it. A man said in it by his opinion what he said. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran from various channels, and the isnad of this from Imran is good."
"3581","3588 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Awf, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Peace be upon you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, he said: Ten good deeds. And another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah. So he returned upon him and said: Twenty good deeds. Then another came and said: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thirty good deeds. And this hadith, similar to its speech has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various channels. And the best isnad narrated in that from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is this isnad, even though one more eminent than Imran narrated it, the isnad of Imran is better."
"3582","3589 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Muslim narrated to us, Bahr ibn Kaniz narrated to us, from Abd Allah al-Laqiti, from Abu Raja, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling weapons in tribulation. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Imran ibn Husayn. And Abd Allah al-Laqiti is not well-known, and Bahr ibn Kaniz was not strong. But we do not retain it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this channel, so we found no escape from bringing it out. And Salm ibn Zarir narrated it from Abu Raja, from Imran, halted."
"3583","3590 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Abu al-Dahma, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you hears of the Dajjal, let him stay away from him, for a man comes to him while he thinks he is a believer or a Muslim, then follows him due to what he sees with him of doubts. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it with this wording except Imran ibn Husayn alone, nor narrating it from Imran except Abu al-Dahma, nor from Abu al-Dahma except Humayd ibn Hilal. And Hisham and Jarir ibn Hazim narrated it from Humayd."
"3584","3591 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Rabah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Sawwar al-Adawi narrated to us, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Modesty is all good. Bushayr ibn Kab said: We find in some books that of it is weakness and of it is dignity. So he said: I informed you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and you narrate to me from the books."
"3585","3592 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is all good. And this hadith was narrated by Amr ibn Ali, from Abu Dawud, from Hammad, from Thabit, from Abu al-Sawwar, from Imran. And we do not know anyone corroborating Amr ibn Ali upon this narration."
"3586","3593 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Abd Allah ibn Nujayd ibn Imran ibn Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3587","3594 - And Muhammad ibn Muawiyah al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Abd Allah ibn Nujayd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: A man of Hudhayl killed a man of Khuzaah in Jahiliyyah, and the Hudhali was hidden. And when the day of the Conquest came, the Hudhali appeared, so a man of Khuzaah met him and slaughtered him as sheep is slaughtered. So he said: Did he kill him before the call or after the call? So they said: After the call. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I been one to kill a believer for a disbeliever, I would have killed him, so bring out his blood-money. So we brought out his blood-money, and it was the first blood-money in Islam. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain more connected than this chain, so for that we wrote it. And Yaqub ibn Abd Allah ibn Nujayd, these are the children of Imran, and even if they did not narrate hadith, the hadith was well-known, disconnected, so these made it connected. And in it is of jurisprudence that everyone given safety, even if disbeliever, his blood-money is the blood-money of a Muslim if the Muslim kills him, and there is no retaliation upon the Muslim in killing him because he is a disbeliever."
"3588","3595 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim, and Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Ata narrated to us, from his father, that Ziyad sent Imran ibn Husayn as a collector, so he came and did not bring anything. So he said to him: Where is the wealth? So he said: We took it as we used to take it upon the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and did as we used to do upon the era of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3589","3596 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to narrate to us most of his night about Banu Israil; he did not stand except for great prayer. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by the narration of Imran ibn Husayn and Abd Allah ibn Amr. And there was disagreement in its isnad from Qatadah, so Abu Hilal said: from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Imran ibn Husayn. And Muadh ibn Hisham said: from his father, from Qatadah, from Abu Hassan, from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Hisham is more retentive than Abu Hilal."
"3590","3597 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Husayn, from al-Shabi, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruqyah except from a poisonous bite. And this hadith, there was disagreement in it from al-Shabi, so Mujalid said: from al-Shabi, from Jabir. And al-Abbas ibn Dharih said: from al-Shabi, from Anas, thus Yazid narrated it from Sharik. And Husayn said: from al-Shabi, from Imran."
"3591","3598 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Rejoice, O Banu Tamim. They said: Since you gave us glad tidings, then give us. So the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed, and peoples of Yemen came, so he said: Accept the glad tidings since Banu Tamim did not accept it. They said: We have accepted it, O Messenger of Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain other than this chain, and its isnad is good."
"3592","3599 - Amr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: And Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah, and Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Muraya, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah."
"3593","3600 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a boy of poor peoples cut the ear of a boy of rich peoples, so his people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We are poor peoples, so he let him go. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Imran ibn Husayn alone. And it has been narrated from Imran from another channel, and this channel is better than the other channel."
"3594","3601 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us the noon prayer, and recited in it: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Which of you contended with me in it, or: which of you is the reciter. So some of the people said: I, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: I knew that some of you contended with me in it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Imran ibn Husayn, and we do not know for it any chain from Imran except this chain, and its isnad is good."
"3595","3602 - Amr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man bit another, so he pulled it, so his front tooth was pulled out. So that was referred to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he nullified it, and said: He wanted to bite the flesh of his brother, or: the flesh of your brother, as the stallion bites. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from other channels, and this is a good isnad from Imran ibn Husayn."
"3596","3603 - Amr narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people, or: the best of this ummah, is the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will arise a people who bear witness and are not asked to bear witness, and vow and do not fulfill, and obesity spreads among them. And this hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from various channels with different wordings, and it has been narrated from Imran from other channels, and this isnad is the best isnad narrated from Imran ibn Husayn for this speech."
"3597","3604 - Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, Shababah narrated to us, from Shubah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Say, O disbelievers, and: Say, He is Allah, One. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrating it from Shubah except Shababah alone, and it is of good isnad."
"3598","3605 - Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hayyaj ibn Imran, that Imran, a boy of his fled, so he made upon himself for Allah that if he overpowers him he will cut his hand. So he sent me to ask Samurah, so I asked him, so he said: Our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge us upon charity and forbid us mutilation. So I came to Imran and asked him, so he said: Our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to urge us upon charity and forbid us mutilation. And this hadith has been narrated from Imran ibn Husayn from other channels, and more than one narrated it from al-Hasan, from Imran, and none inserted between Imran and al-Hasan anyone other than Qatadah."
"3599","3606 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Amr ibn Ubayd informed us, from Abu Raja al-Utaridi, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his family never ate to satiety morning and evening of barley bread until he met his Lord."
"3600","3607 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan, the nephew of Salim ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, he said: Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever aids his brother in absence while he is able to aid him, Allah will aid him in this world and the Hereafter."
